00:01:24.351 --> 00:01:25.702
- Oh this guy.
- Mr. Stark.


00:01:26.258 --> 00:01:27.122
Hey.


00:01:27.147 --> 00:01:29.248
She's going to need a cardiologist
right away.


00:01:30.456 --> 00:01:31.885
- Bye!
- Perhaps another time?


00:01:33.044 --> 00:01:36.150
It started in Bern,
Switzerland, 1999.


00:01:38.503 --> 00:01:39.670
The old days.


00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:42.272
I never thought they'd come back to bite me.


00:01:43.511 --> 00:01:47.607
Hey Tony! Aldrich Killian,
I'm a big fan of your work.


00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:49.206
- My work?
- Who isn't? She needs me.


00:01:49.207 --> 00:01:52.700
Well, of course, but Miss
Hansen my organization


00:01:52.701 --> 00:01:55.477
has been tracking your research since
year two of MIT.


00:01:56.849 --> 00:01:58.690
Oh wow, he made it.
He made the cut.


00:01:58.691 --> 00:02:01.642
- What floor you going to, pal?
- Well now, that is an appropriate question.


00:02:01.728 --> 00:02:04.928
The ground floor, actually, of a proposal
I'm putting together myself.


00:02:04.956 --> 00:02:08.556
It's a privately-funded think tank called
"Advanced Idea Mechanics".


00:02:09.068 --> 00:02:12.638
Uh, she'll take both. One to throw
