00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:16.070
"Advanced Idea Mechanics" or AIM
for short, you get it?


00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:18.281
I see that 'cause it's on
your T-shirt.


00:02:18.306 --> 00:02:18.848
Oh!!


00:02:19.149 --> 00:02:21.787
Ladies, follow the mullet.
Ladies first.


00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:22.883
Thank you. I'll call you.


00:02:26.251 --> 00:02:28.919
I am titillated by the notion
of working with you. - Yeah?


00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:29.998
I'm going to ditch
these clowns.


00:02:30.023 --> 00:02:31.224
I'll see you up on the roof
in five minutes.


00:02:31.334 --> 00:02:34.186
I'm just going to try to get my beef wet real quick
if you know what I'm talkin' about.


00:02:34.568 --> 00:02:35.431
I'll see you up there!


00:02:35.451 --> 00:02:36.383
Damn betcha.


00:02:37.083 --> 00:02:40.164
- Come on, I thought that was just a theory.
- Well... it was.


00:02:40.364 --> 00:02:42.819
If I'm right, we can access the area
of the brain


00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:46.068
that governs repair and chemically recode it.
- That's incredible.


00:02:46.139 --> 00:02:49.911
Essentially, you're hacking into the genetic
operating system of a


00:02:49.912 --> 00:02:51.015
- living organism.
- Exactly.


00:02:52.122 --> 00:02:56.234
Can you not touch my plant?
It's not... she doesn't like it. She perfers -


00:02:56.314 --> 00:02:57.423
She's not like the others.


00:02:57.424 --> 00:02:58.916
Come on, let's go to
the bedroom.


00:02:58.917 --> 00:03:01.127
Happy, leave her
ficus alone.


00:03:01.828 --> 00:03:02.838
No, seriously, don't


00:03:02.839 --> 00:03:05.509
- And you're starting with plants?
- For now, yes.


00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:07.020
I'm calling it "Extremis".


00:03:07.221 --> 00:03:10.362
- Well, its -
- Human application.


00:03:10.503 --> 00:03:13.414
Exactly! Exactly!
Dentra-degree vitalization.


00:03:13.635 --> 00:03:15.256
Disease prevention.


00:03:15.424 --> 00:03:16.489
Even limb regrowth.


00:03:18.407 --> 00:03:19.939
You're the most gifted woman
I've ever met.


00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:22.029
- Wow!
- In Switzerland.


00:03:22.030 --> 00:03:25.191
- That's better.
- This week.


00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:27.642
You almost bought it,
didn't you?


00:03:38.168 --> 00:03:40.520
This is what I'm talking
about, the glitch.


00:03:40.521 --> 00:03:42.030
Have you checked the telomerase
algorithm?


00:03:45.103 --> 00:03:46.674
- We're good.
- Stay down.


00:03:46.675 --> 00:03:48.874
You're right on me...


00:03:49.765 --> 00:03:50.996
What the hell was that?


00:03:52.798 --> 00:03:53.792
What the hell was that?


00:03:53.793 --> 00:03:54.476
It's a glitch in my work.


00:03:54.877 --> 00:03:56.869
She was just talking about it.
Glitches happen.


00:03:56.870 --> 00:03:58.410
Oh, it's not Y2K...


00:03:58.501 --> 00:03:59.966
Hey, Happy New
Year!


00:03:59.967 --> 00:04:00.821
- Happy New Year.
- Happy New Year.


00:04:00.822 --> 00:04:02.963
Alright, I'll see you in the morning,
Okay? Good night.


00:04:02.964 --> 00:04:03.315
You good?


00:04:03.316 --> 00:04:04.824
- Yep. - I'll be right outside.
- Okay, cool.


00:04:25.149 --> 00:04:30.690
So, why am I telling you this? Because I
had just created demons.


00:04:31.808 --> 00:04:33.240
And I didn't even know it.


00:04:35.793 --> 00:04:37.993
Yeah, those were good times.


00:04:38.904 --> 00:04:40.145
Then I moved on.


00:04:40.956 --> 00:04:45.027
After a brief soiree in an Afghan cave,
I said "Goodbye" to the party scene.


00:04:45.127 --> 00:04:47.409
I forgot that night in Switzerland.


00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:49.580
These days I'm a changed man.


00:04:49.611 --> 00:04:51.442
I'm different now.


00:04:52.061 --> 00:04:54.864
I'm... well, you know
who I am.


00:04:55.583 --> 00:04:56.833
Sir, please may I request


00:04:56.834 --> 00:04:59.656
just a few hours to calibrate -
- Nope!


00:05:03.599 --> 00:05:05.499
Micro-repeater implanting
sequence complete!


00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:07.326
As you wish, sir. I've
also prepared a


00:05:07.327 --> 00:05:09.340
safety briefing for you
to enitrely ignore.


00:05:09.341 --> 00:05:10.992
Which I will.


00:05:10.993 --> 00:05:12.413
Alright, let's do this.


00:05:12.984 --> 00:05:17.386
Dummy. Hi Dummy.
How did you get that cap on your head?


00:05:17.387 --> 00:05:18.496
You earned it.


00:05:18.521 --> 00:05:19.822
Hey. Hey!


00:05:21.739 --> 00:05:23.270
What are you doing out of the corner?
You know what you did.


00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:25.612
Blood on my mat, handle it.


00:05:26.472 --> 00:05:29.834
Sir, may I remind you that you've been
awake for nearly 72 hours.


00:05:30.885 --> 00:05:32.996
Focus up ladies.
Good evening


00:05:33.196 --> 00:05:34.807
And welcome to the
birthing suite.


00:05:35.107 --> 00:05:37.553
I am pleased to announce the
imminent arrival


00:05:37.654 --> 00:05:40.421
of your bouncing,
badass baby brother.


00:05:41.233 --> 00:05:43.675
Start titan and go white.
Stamp date and time.


00:05:44.695 --> 00:05:47.545
Mark 42 autonomous prehensile
propulsion suit test.


00:05:48.082 --> 00:05:49.149
Initialize sequence.


00:05:51.627 --> 00:05:53.447
Jarvis, drop my needle.


00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:18.522
Crap.


00:06:36.983 --> 00:06:39.004
Alright, I think we got this.
Send them all.


00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:51.572
Probably just a little fast, slow it down.
Slow it down just a... little bit.


00:06:59.296 --> 00:07:01.158
Cool it, will you Jarvis?


00:07:11.423 --> 00:07:12.682
Come on.


00:07:13.275 --> 00:07:14.576
I ain't scared of you.


00:07:21.510 --> 00:07:23.350
I'm the best.


00:07:29.964 --> 00:07:33.546
As always sir, a great pleasure
watching you work.


00:07:33.577 --> 00:07:37.247
I guess 72 hours is a long
time between siestas.


00:07:37.508 --> 00:07:40.319
Didn't think it could
get any worse.


00:07:41.240 --> 00:07:42.852
Then they had to go and
turn on the TV.


00:07:46.783 --> 00:07:48.564
That's when 'He' happened.


00:07:57.441 --> 00:07:59.701
Some people call me a terrorist.


00:08:02.623 --> 00:08:04.744
I consider myself a teacher.


00:08:07.435 --> 00:08:09.267
America...


00:08:10.537 --> 00:08:13.779
Ready for another lesson.


00:08:13.780 --> 00:08:16.631
In 1864 in Sand Creek, Colorado.


00:08:16.831 --> 00:08:21.683
The U.S. military waited until the friendly
Cheyenne Braves had all gone hunting.


00:08:21.783 --> 00:08:25.936
Waited to attack and slaughter
the families left behind.


00:08:26.036 --> 00:08:29.568
And claim their land.


00:08:29.569 --> 00:08:35.663
39 hours ago, the Ali Al Salem Air Base
in Kuwait was attacked.


00:08:36.533 --> 00:08:38.724
I did that.


00:08:38.725 --> 00:08:42.466
A quaint military church, filled with
wives and children of course.


00:08:44.947 --> 00:08:48.149
The soliders were out
on manuvers.


00:08:49.660 --> 00:08:52.732
The "Braves" were away.


00:08:53.003 --> 00:08:58.326
President Ellis, you continue to resist
my attempts to educate you, sir.


00:08:58.526 --> 00:09:00.748
And now, you've missed
me again.


00:09:03.838 --> 00:09:08.091
You know who I am.
You don't know where I am.


00:09:09.441 --> 00:09:12.374
And you'll never
see me coming.


00:09:15.465 --> 00:09:18.087
... and now that we seem to be back,
let's recap some of the frightening developments in this story.


00:09:18.307 --> 00:09:20.399
American airways
were hijacked.


00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:21.920
The nation remains
on high alert.


00:09:21.921 --> 00:09:24.490
All attempts to find the Mandarin have
so far proved unsuccessful.


00:09:24.590 --> 00:09:29.514
Central to my administration's response to this
terrorist event is a newly-minted resource.


00:09:30.395 --> 00:09:33.396
I know him as Colonel
James Rhodes.


00:09:33.696 --> 00:09:37.228
The American people will soon
know him as the Iron Patriot.


00:09:37.467 --> 00:09:40.270
And how is President
Ellis responding?


00:09:40.551 --> 00:09:44.723
By taking the guy they call "War Machine"
and giving him a paint job.


00:09:44.724 --> 00:09:48.976
The same suit but painted red,
white and blue, look at that.


00:09:48.977 --> 00:09:51.876
And they've also renamed
him Iron Patriot.


00:09:51.976 --> 00:09:55.408
You know, just in case the
paint was too subtle.


00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:57.430
It tested well with focus
groups, alright?


00:09:57.431 --> 00:09:59.201
- I am Iron Patriot.
- Listen.


00:09:59.202 --> 00:10:01.189
War Machine was a little too
aggressive, alright.


00:10:01.190 --> 00:10:02.332
This sends a better message.


00:10:04.464 --> 00:10:07.866
So what's really going on?
With Mandarin.


00:10:08.717 --> 00:10:11.398
Seriously, can we talk
about this guy?


00:10:14.059 --> 00:10:16.560
It's classified information,
Tony.


00:10:16.991 --> 00:10:19.743
- Okay, there've been nine bombings.
- Nine.


00:10:19.744 --> 00:10:21.375
The public only knows about three.


00:10:21.376 --> 00:10:24.515
But here's the thing...
nobody can ID a device.


00:10:24.786 --> 00:10:25.987
There's no bomb casings.


00:10:25.988 --> 00:10:27.097
You know I can help.


00:10:27.098 --> 00:10:31.570
Just ask. I got a ton of new tech.
I got a prehensile suit. I got


00:10:31.571 --> 00:10:32.091
Bomb disposal.


00:10:32.092 --> 00:10:33.532
Catches explosions mid-air.


00:10:33.533 --> 00:10:35.334
When's the last time you got
a good night's sleep?


00:10:35.335 --> 00:10:38.203
Einstein slept three hours a year.
Look what he did.


00:10:38.204 --> 00:10:39.349
People are concerned about
you, Tony.


00:10:39.350 --> 00:10:40.395
I'm concerned about you.


00:10:40.585 --> 00:10:41.573
You gonna come at
me like that?


00:10:41.574 --> 00:10:43.437
No, look, I'm not trying
to be a dic-


00:10:44.467 --> 00:10:46.638
-tator.
- Would you mind signing my drawing?


00:10:46.639 --> 00:10:49.275
If Richard doesn't mind. You alright
with this, Dick?


00:10:49.776 --> 00:10:50.672
Fine with me.


00:10:52.461 --> 00:10:53.944
- What is your name?
- Erin.


00:10:55.545 --> 00:10:57.976
I loved you in "A Christmas Story"
by the way.


00:10:58.866 --> 00:11:00.937
Listen, the Pentagon
is scared.


00:11:01.177 --> 00:11:03.907
After New York, aliens,
come on.


00:11:03.908 --> 00:11:05.319
They need to look strong.


00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:08.612
Stopping the Mandarin is a
priority, but it's not-


00:11:09.013 --> 00:11:10.422
It's not superhero business.


00:11:10.423 --> 00:11:11.324
No, it's not. Quite frankly.


00:11:11.325 --> 00:11:12.714
It's American business.


00:11:12.739 --> 00:11:14.840
That's why I said.
I...got it.


00:11:14.976 --> 00:11:16.236
Are you okay?


00:11:17.196 --> 00:11:18.418
I broke the crayon.


00:11:18.419 --> 00:11:20.048
Are you okay,
Mr. Stark?


00:11:20.049 --> 00:11:22.188
Take it easy. Tony...


00:11:23.130 --> 00:11:25.311
How did you get out
of the wormhole?


00:11:26.221 --> 00:11:28.043
- Tony
- What did you say?


00:11:29.583 --> 00:11:34.236
Sorry. Have to check on
the suit... make sure...okay.


00:11:37.689 --> 00:11:40.310
Check the heart, check the,
check the, is it the brain?


00:11:40.570 --> 00:11:43.602
No sign of cardiac analomy
or unusual brain activity.


00:11:43.723 --> 00:11:45.624
Okay, so I was
poisoned?


00:11:45.913 --> 00:11:50.426
My diagnosis is that you've experienced
a severe anxiety attack.


00:11:53.317 --> 00:11:54.058
Me?


00:11:55.019 --> 00:11:56.819
Come on man, this isn't a
good look. Open up.


00:11:56.820 --> 00:11:57.970
Sorry, I gotta split.


00:12:00.972 --> 00:12:06.585
Badge... Badge... Badge.


00:12:07.385 --> 00:12:09.967
Badge, guys. I put a memo in
the toliet, come on.


00:12:10.217 --> 00:12:12.087
Tony has got them in his basement,
they're wearing


00:12:12.088 --> 00:12:14.029
party hats, this is an asset
we can put to use.


00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:16.269
Uh-huh. So, you're suggesting
that I replace


00:12:16.370 --> 00:12:18.553
the entire janitorial
staff with robots?


00:12:18.802 --> 00:12:21.704
What I'm saying is that the human
element of Human


00:12:21.705 --> 00:12:23.715
Resources is our biggest
point of vulnerability.


00:12:23.716 --> 00:12:25.556
We should start phasing it
out immediately.


00:12:25.946 --> 00:12:27.477
- What!?
- Excuse me, Bambi


00:12:27.768 --> 00:12:29.840
- Did you just say that?
- Security


00:12:29.841 --> 00:12:33.209
Happy, okay, I am thrilled that you're
now the Head of Security.


00:12:33.210 --> 00:12:34.952
Okay, it is the perfect position for you.
- Thank you.


00:12:34.953 --> 00:12:36.522
- However,
- I do appreciate it.


00:12:36.523 --> 00:12:39.024
- Since you've taken the post,
- You don't have to thank me.


00:12:39.025 --> 00:12:42.126
We've had a rise in staff complaints
of 300 percent.


00:12:42.135 --> 00:12:44.787
- Thank you.
- That's not a compliment.


00:12:44.788 --> 00:12:46.638
"That's not a compliment"?
It is a compliment!


00:12:46.639 --> 00:12:48.449
Clearly somebody is trying
to hide something.


00:12:48.474 --> 00:12:49.299
- Excuse me.
- Yes?


00:12:49.300 --> 00:12:51.461
Miss Potts, your four o'clock
is here.


00:12:51.462 --> 00:12:53.150
Did you clear this four o'clock
with me?


00:12:53.151 --> 00:12:54.603
Happy, we'll talk about
this later


00:12:54.604 --> 00:12:57.235
But right now I have to go deal with
this very annoying thing.


00:12:57.236 --> 00:12:58.495
How so?


00:12:59.456 --> 00:13:00.668
I used to work with him, and he
used to ask me


00:13:00.669 --> 00:13:02.478
out all the time, so it's a
little awkward.


00:13:02.578 --> 00:13:03.939
I don't like the
sound of that.


00:13:09.873 --> 00:13:12.614
- Pepper.
- Killian?


00:13:12.615 --> 00:13:15.356
You look great...
you look really great.


00:13:15.724 --> 00:13:18.463
God, you look great.


00:13:18.464 --> 00:13:21.779
I... I... I can't...What on Earth have
you been doing?


00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:25.151
Nothing fancy, just five years in the
hands of physical therapists


00:13:25.152 --> 00:13:27.372
And please, call me Aldrich.


00:13:27.963 --> 00:13:30.036
Uh, you were supposed to be
issued a security badge?


00:13:30.037 --> 00:13:30.804
Happy, it's okay.


00:13:30.805 --> 00:13:32.205
- Yes?
- We're good.


00:13:32.206 --> 00:13:33.526
- You sure?
- Yes.


00:13:33.527 --> 00:13:35.307
- Stand down.
- I'm going to linger.


00:13:35.308 --> 00:13:36.738
- Thank you.
- Right here, okay.


00:13:36.739 --> 00:13:38.568
It's very nice to see
you, Killian.


00:13:45.843 --> 00:13:47.554
Hey, guy


00:13:55.119 --> 00:13:56.079
Merry Christmas.


00:13:56.664 --> 00:14:01.047
After years dodging the president's ban
on "Immoral Biotech Research",


00:14:01.347 --> 00:14:06.907
My think tank now has a little
something in the pipeline.


00:14:07.809 --> 00:14:12.104
It's an idea we like to call
"Extremis".


00:14:13.061 --> 00:14:14.677
I'm gonna turn your
lights down.


00:14:17.117 --> 00:14:19.170
Regard the human brain.


00:14:25.640 --> 00:14:28.901
Uh, wait, hold on, hold on, that's, that's
the universe, my bad.


00:14:28.902 --> 00:14:30.582
But if I do that...


00:14:35.627 --> 00:14:39.607
That's the brain, strangely memetic
though, wouldn't you say?


00:14:39.749 --> 00:14:41.926
- Wow, that's amazing!
- Thanks, it's mine.


00:14:43.015 --> 00:14:46.138
- What?
- This... you're inside my head.


00:14:46.139 --> 00:14:49.786
It's a live feed. Come on up,
I'll prove it to you.


00:14:51.988 --> 00:14:53.497
Come on.


00:14:56.083 --> 00:14:59.680
Now, pinch my arm. I can take it.
Pinch me.


00:15:01.932 --> 00:15:02.816
What is that?


00:15:02.817 --> 00:15:04.894
The primary somatosensory
cortex.


00:15:04.994 --> 00:15:10.039
It's the brain's pain center, but this...
is what I wanted to show you.


00:15:12.434 --> 00:15:16.080
Now, "Extremis" harnesses our
bioelectrical potential.


00:15:16.677 --> 00:15:18.759
And it goes... here.


00:15:19.050 --> 00:15:22.940
This is essentially an empty slot,
and what this tells us is that


00:15:22.941 --> 00:15:27.732
our mind, our entire DNA in fact,
is destined to be upgraded.


00:15:28.158 --> 00:15:29.158
Wow.


00:15:37.930 --> 00:15:41.013
Hello? Is this forehead
of Security?


00:15:41.019 --> 00:15:42.939
What? You know, look, I got a real job.
What do you want?


00:15:42.940 --> 00:15:44.396
I'm working. I got something
going on here.


00:15:44.397 --> 00:15:45.993
- What? Harassing interns?
- Let me tell you something,


00:15:45.994 --> 00:15:47.964
You know what happened when I told people
I was Iron Man's bodyguard?


00:15:47.965 --> 00:15:49.587
They would laugh
in my face.


00:15:50.145 --> 00:15:52.046
I had to leave while I still
had a shred of dignity.


00:15:52.359 --> 00:15:54.770
Now I got a real job. I'm
watching Pepper.


00:15:54.840 --> 00:15:55.985
What's going on?
Fill me in.


00:15:56.551 --> 00:15:57.476
- For real?
- Yeah.


00:15:57.776 --> 00:16:00.895
Alright, so she's meeting up with this
scientist rich guy, handsome.


00:16:00.896 --> 00:16:02.432
I couldn't make his face
at first, right?


00:16:02.433 --> 00:16:03.370
And you know I'm good
with faces.


00:16:03.371 --> 00:16:05.688
- Oh yeah, you're the best.
- Yeah, so I run his credentials


00:16:05.689 --> 00:16:08.604
I make him Aldrich Killian. We actually
met the guy back in -


00:16:08.648 --> 00:16:11.206
Where were we in '99? The
Science Conference?


00:16:11.210 --> 00:16:13.388
Uh,  Switzerland.


00:16:13.389 --> 00:16:13.943
Right, right, exactly.


00:16:13.944 --> 00:16:16.147
- Killian, I don't remember that guy.
- Of course you don't remember,


00:16:16.148 --> 00:16:17.199
he's not a blonde with a big rack.


00:16:17.231 --> 00:16:19.496
At first it was fine, they were
talking business, but now


00:16:19.497 --> 00:16:22.105
it's like getting weird. He's showing
her his big brain.


00:16:22.205 --> 00:16:25.063
- His what?
- Big brain, and she likes it.


00:16:25.064 --> 00:16:27.285
Here, let me show you.
Hold on. See?


00:16:27.585 --> 00:16:31.258
Look at what? You watching them? Flip the
screen and then we can get started.


00:16:31.259 --> 00:16:34.331
I'm not a tech genius like you, just
trust me, get down here.


00:16:34.332 --> 00:16:35.881
Flip the screen, then I can see
what they're doing.


00:16:35.882 --> 00:16:37.246
I don't know how to flip
the screen!


00:16:37.247 --> 00:16:39.594
Don't talk to me like that anymore.
You're not my boss.


00:16:39.895 --> 00:16:43.747
Alright, I don't work for you, and
I don't trust this guy.


00:16:43.748 --> 00:16:45.548
He's got another guy with
him, he's shifty.


00:16:45.569 --> 00:16:47.749
Relax. I'm just asking you to
secure the perimeter.


00:16:47.750 --> 00:16:49.436
Tell him to go out for a
drink or something.


00:16:49.437 --> 00:16:51.537
You know what? You should take more
of an interest in what's going on here.


00:16:51.538 --> 00:16:53.433
This woman is the best thing
that ever happened to you.


00:16:53.434 --> 00:16:55.356
- And you're just ignoring her.
- A giant brain?


00:16:55.357 --> 00:16:57.483
Yeah, there's a giant brain,
there's a shifty character...


00:16:57.484 --> 00:16:58.968
I'm going to follow this guy.
I'm going to run


00:16:58.969 --> 00:17:01.576
his plates and if it
gets rough, so be it.


00:17:02.377 --> 00:17:03.311
I miss you, Happy.


00:17:03.312 --> 00:17:05.693
Yeah, I miss you too but the
way it used to be.


00:17:05.789 --> 00:17:06.931
Now you're off with
the 'superfriends'


00:17:06.932 --> 00:17:08.486
I don't know what's going on
with you anymore.


00:17:08.487 --> 00:17:09.379
The world's gettin' weird.


00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:11.693
Hey I hate to cut you off, do you have
your taser on you?- Why?


00:17:11.694 --> 00:17:12.900
I think there's a gal in HR
who is trying


00:17:12.901 --> 00:17:16.356
to steal some printer ink. You should probably
go over there and zap her.


00:17:16.381 --> 00:17:17.439
Yeah, nice.


00:17:17.440 --> 00:17:20.726
Imagine if you could hack into
the hard drive of


00:17:20.727 --> 00:17:23.799
any living organism and
recode its DNA.


00:17:24.527 --> 00:17:25.851
It would be incredible.


00:17:26.521 --> 00:17:30.299
Unfortunately, to my ears it also
sounds highly weaponizable.


00:17:30.300 --> 00:17:34.218
As in enhanced soldiers, private
armies, and Tony is not -


00:17:34.219 --> 00:17:35.431
Tony, Tony.


00:17:36.232 --> 00:17:38.686
You know, I invited Tony
to join AIM.


00:17:39.286 --> 00:17:43.174
13 years ago and he
turned me down.


00:17:43.226 --> 00:17:48.209
But something tells me now there is a new genius
on the throne, who doesn't have to


00:17:48.211 --> 00:17:52.669
answer to Tony anymore and who
has slightly less of an ego.


00:17:54.108 --> 00:17:59.381
It's going to be a no, Aldrich...
as much as I'd like to help you.


00:18:01.435 --> 00:18:06.700
I can't say that I'm not disappointed,
but as my father used to say,


00:18:06.701 --> 00:18:09.013
"Failure is the fog through which
we glimpse triumph."


00:18:09.014 --> 00:18:12.893
It's very deep, and I have no
idea what it means.


00:18:12.894 --> 00:18:15.089
Well, he was kind of an
idiot, my old man.


00:18:16.311 --> 00:18:18.373
I'm sure I'll see you again,
Pepper.


00:18:29.303 --> 00:18:30.256
Happy!


00:18:31.058 --> 00:18:33.965
The car is ready... if you're
ready to go.


00:18:35.613 --> 00:18:42.506
Yes, I just um, God, I forgot my other
thing so I'm just gonna...


00:19:10.294 --> 00:19:13.845
I'm sorry I'm late. I was..
What is that?!


00:19:14.380 --> 00:19:18.097
You're wearing this in the house now?
What is that, like Mark 15?


00:19:18.098 --> 00:19:21.857
Yeah, something like that. You know
everybody needs a hobby.


00:19:22.033 --> 00:19:24.708
Oh, and you have to wear your hobby
in the living room?


00:19:24.809 --> 00:19:29.190
Just breaking it in, you know, it's always a little
pinchy in the GUI-bagger at first.


00:19:29.201 --> 00:19:31.622
Oh hey, did you see your
Christmas present?


00:19:31.623 --> 00:19:35.927
Yes, I did. I don't know how I could have
missed that Christmas present.


00:19:35.928 --> 00:19:37.544
Is it gonna fit through
the door?


00:19:37.545 --> 00:19:39.759
Well actually, uh, that's a good question,
I got a team of


00:19:39.760 --> 00:19:41.859
guys coming tomorrow. They're gonna
blow out that wall.


00:19:41.866 --> 00:19:44.455
So, uh, tense?
Good day?


00:19:45.269 --> 00:19:47.098
Oh shoulders, a little naughty.
Naughty girl.


00:19:47.412 --> 00:19:51.023
I don't want to harp on this, but did you
like the custom rabbit?


00:19:51.969 --> 00:19:53.115
Did I like it?


00:19:53.116 --> 00:19:54.707
- Nailed it, right?
- Wow.


00:19:54.781 --> 00:19:57.786
I appreciate the thought
very much.


00:19:58.287 --> 00:20:02.620
So why don't you lift up that facemask
and give me a kiss.


00:20:03.339 --> 00:20:06.825
Huh, yup, damnit.
No can do.


00:20:07.326 --> 00:20:11.330
You want to just kiss it on
the, uh, facial slit?


00:20:11.430 --> 00:20:13.723
Why don't I run down to the
garage and see if


00:20:13.724 --> 00:20:15.768
I can't find a crowbar to jimmy
that thing open?


00:20:15.769 --> 00:20:19.942
A crowbar? Yeah. Oh, except there's
been a radiation leak.


00:20:19.943 --> 00:20:21.817
- I'll take my chances.
- That's risky.


00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:24.855
At least let me get you
like a Hazmat suit.


00:20:26.354 --> 00:20:27.923
Or a Geiger counter or
something like that.


00:20:30.027 --> 00:20:33.754
- Busted.
- This is a new level of lame.


00:20:33.755 --> 00:20:37.021
- Sorry.
- You ate without me, already? On date night?


00:20:37.505 --> 00:20:39.078
- He was just.
- You mean you.


00:20:39.374 --> 00:20:41.338
Well yeah, I just mean
we were just...


00:20:41.339 --> 00:20:44.204
just hosting you while I
finished up a little work.


00:20:44.229 --> 00:20:44.540
Uh Huh..


00:20:44.541 --> 00:20:47.120
And yes, I had a quick bite. I didn't know
if you were coming home


00:20:47.167 --> 00:20:49.241
Or you were having drinks with
Aldrich Killian.


00:20:52.277 --> 00:20:53.136
What?


00:20:54.437 --> 00:20:57.077
Aldrich Killian? What are you
checking up on me?


00:20:57.078 --> 00:20:58.974
- Happy was concerned.
- No, you're spying on me.


00:20:58.975 --> 00:21:02.705
- I'm going to bed.
- Hold on. Come on. Pep-


00:21:02.905 --> 00:21:06.417
Hey, I admit it! My fault.
Sorry.


00:21:06.925 --> 00:21:08.881
I'm a piping hot mess.


00:21:11.283 --> 00:21:13.925
It's been going on for a while...
I haven't said anything.


00:21:15.999 --> 00:21:19.298
- Nothing's been the same since New York.
- Oh really?


00:21:20.206 --> 00:21:22.230
I didn't notice
that, at all.


00:21:22.344 --> 00:21:27.246
You experience things and then they're over
and you still can't explain them.


00:21:27.707 --> 00:21:31.309
Gods, aliens, other dimensions...
I'm just a man in a can.


00:21:32.403 --> 00:21:36.156
The only reason I haven't cracked up is
probably because you've moved in.


00:21:36.157 --> 00:21:38.662
Which is great. I love
you, I'm lucky.


00:21:39.068 --> 00:21:42.581
But honey... I can't sleep.


00:21:43.060 --> 00:21:47.483
You go to bed, I come down here.
I do what I know, I tinker.


00:21:48.986 --> 00:21:51.101
The threat is imminent.


00:21:51.102 --> 00:21:53.744
And I have to protect the one thing
that I can't live without.


00:21:54.944 --> 00:21:58.413
That's you. And my suits,
they're uh...


00:21:58.685 --> 00:22:00.891
- Machines.
- They're part of me.


00:22:02.533 --> 00:22:06.051
- A distraction.
- Maybe.


00:22:23.422 --> 00:22:26.750
- I'm gonna take a shower.
- Okay.


00:22:30.008 --> 00:22:33.846
- And you're going to join me.
- Better.


00:22:52.522 --> 00:22:53.814
Tony!


00:23:02.427 --> 00:23:04.045
Power down!


00:23:11.465 --> 00:23:15.523
I must have called it in my sleep.
That's not supposed to happen.


00:23:18.575 --> 00:23:20.908
I'll recalibrate the sensors.


00:23:22.412 --> 00:23:28.738
Can we just...just let me...just let me catch my
breath, okay? Don't go, alright? Pepper?


00:23:28.739 --> 00:23:31.749
I'm going to sleep downstairs.
Tinker with that.


00:23:58.597 --> 00:24:01.205
- Can you regulate?
- Yes, I can regulate.


00:24:01.206 --> 00:24:03.146
- Are you sure about that?
- Yes.


00:24:12.824 --> 00:24:14.549
It's a decent batch.


00:24:15.734 --> 00:24:17.863
Don't say I never did
nothing for you.


00:24:17.864 --> 00:24:21.841
Thank you. I mean for
understanding.


00:24:31.288 --> 00:24:32.676
I'm sorry, buddy.


00:24:48.168 --> 00:24:49.341
What're ya doing, buddy?


00:24:49.650 --> 00:24:52.260
You out by yourself? A little date night? Watching
your favorite chick flick maybe?


00:24:52.825 --> 00:24:54.730
Yeah, a little movie called
"The Party's Over"


00:24:54.731 --> 00:24:57.848
Starring you and your junkie girlfriend,
and here's the ticket.


00:24:57.849 --> 00:25:00.132
No kidding. That doesn't
belong to you.


00:25:26.396 --> 00:25:31.330
Savin! Help!
Help me!


00:26:56.852 --> 00:26:59.310
A true story about fortune cookies.


00:26:59.610 --> 00:27:02.974
They look Chinese. They
sound Chinese.


00:27:04.144 --> 00:27:07.689
But they're actually an
American invention.


00:27:08.015 --> 00:27:15.251
Which is why they're hollow, full of lies,
and leave a bad taste in the mouth.


00:27:16.397 --> 00:27:21.369
My disciples just destroyed another
cheap American knock-off.


00:27:21.569 --> 00:27:26.492
The Chinese Theater.
Mr. President.


00:27:26.870 --> 00:27:30.058
I know this must be
getting frustrating.


00:27:30.458 --> 00:27:34.053
But this season of terror is
drawing to a close.


00:27:34.818 --> 00:27:41.172
And don't worry, the big one is
coming, your graduation.


00:27:55.514 --> 00:27:57.162
- Hi.
- Oh, uh.


00:27:57.287 --> 00:27:59.288
- Mind leaving that on?
- Sure.


00:28:06.068 --> 00:28:09.300
Sunday night's PBS,
"Downtown Abbey"


00:28:11.543 --> 00:28:12.977
That's the show. He thinks
it's elegant.


00:28:17.032 --> 00:28:19.555
One more thing, make sure everyone wears
their badges. He's a stickler


00:28:19.556 --> 00:28:22.010
for that sort of thing, plus my guys won't
let anyone in without them.


00:28:23.219 --> 00:28:25.362
We're awaiting the arrival
of Tony Stark.


00:28:25.363 --> 00:28:27.453
We're hoping he'll give
us the reaction.


00:28:27.454 --> 00:28:29.476
His reaction to the
latest attack.


00:28:29.477 --> 00:28:31.096
Mr. Stark!


00:28:31.573 --> 00:28:35.134
Our sources are telling us that this is
another Mandarin attack.


00:28:35.135 --> 00:28:36.934
Anything else you can tell us?


00:28:37.297 --> 00:28:42.301
Hey Mr. Stark! When is somebody going
to kill this guy? Just sayin'.


00:28:44.943 --> 00:28:46.671
Is that what you want?


00:28:49.192 --> 00:28:52.890
Here's a little Holiday greeting I've been
wanting to send to the Mandarin.


00:28:53.263 --> 00:28:55.831
I just didn't know how to
phrase it until now.


00:28:56.638 --> 00:28:59.202
My name is Tony Stark and
I'm not afraid of you.


00:28:59.541 --> 00:29:02.608
I know that you're a coward,
so I've decided


00:29:03.499 --> 00:29:05.520
That you just died, pal.


00:29:05.521 --> 00:29:07.346
I'm gonna come get the body.


00:29:07.347 --> 00:29:10.461
There's no politics here, it's just good
old-fashioned revenge.


00:29:10.694 --> 00:29:12.964
There's no Pentagon. It's just
you and me.


00:29:13.319 --> 00:29:17.012
And on the off-chance you're a man,
here's my home address:


00:29:17.013 --> 00:29:22.456
10880, Malibu Port, 90265.


00:29:22.979 --> 00:29:26.616
I'll leave the door unlocked. That's what
you wanted, right?


00:29:29.374 --> 00:29:30.840
Bill me.


00:29:35.700 --> 00:29:37.731
I've compiled a Mandarin
database for you, sir.


00:29:38.828 --> 00:29:42.401
Drawn from S.H.I.E.L.D., F.B.I.
and C.I.A. intercepts.


00:29:42.811 --> 00:29:45.729
Initiating virtual crimescene
reconstruction.


00:29:47.875 --> 00:29:50.500
Okay, what do we got here?


00:29:50.938 --> 00:29:53.550
His name is an ancient
Chinese war mantle


00:29:53.812 --> 00:29:55.130
Meaning "Advisor to the King".


00:29:55.938 --> 00:29:57.944
South American insurgency tactics.


00:29:58.645 --> 00:30:00.338
Talks like a Bapist
preacher.


00:30:01.215 --> 00:30:04.559
There's lots of pagentry going
on here, lots of theatre.


00:30:05.491 --> 00:30:09.588
Close. - The heat from the blast was
in excess of 3000 degrees Celsius.


00:30:09.954 --> 00:30:13.304
Any subjects within 12.5 yards
were vaporized instantly.


00:30:13.726 --> 00:30:17.186
No bomb parts found in a 3-mile radius
of the Chinese theatre. - No, sir.


00:30:19.542 --> 00:30:21.036
Talk to me, Happy.


00:30:39.632 --> 00:30:42.038
When is a bomb not a bomb?


00:30:52.596 --> 00:30:56.055
- Any military victims?
- Not according to public records, sir.


00:30:56.555 --> 00:31:00.127
Bring up the thermogenic signatures
again, factor in 3000 degrees.


00:31:00.128 --> 00:31:02.738
The oracle cloud has
completed analysis.


00:31:02.909 --> 00:31:07.904
Accessing satellites and plotting the last 12
months of thermogenic occurances now.


00:31:09.005 --> 00:31:11.749
Take away everywhere that there's
been a Mandarin attack.


00:31:16.398 --> 00:31:17.566
Nope.


00:31:24.428 --> 00:31:26.252
That. You sure that's
not one of his?


00:31:26.253 --> 00:31:28.666
It predates any known
Mandarin attack.


00:31:28.667 --> 00:31:31.709
The incident was the use of a
bomb to assist a suicide.


00:31:31.734 --> 00:31:32.735
Bring it around.


00:31:33.510 --> 00:31:38.756
The heat signature is remarkably similar.
3000 degrees Celsius.


00:31:40.267 --> 00:31:42.179
That's two military guys.


00:31:43.372 --> 00:31:44.841
Ever been to Tennessee, Jarvis?


00:31:44.842 --> 00:31:46.957
Creating a flight plan for Tennessee.


00:31:52.796 --> 00:31:58.085
Are we still at 'Ding-Dong'? We're supposed
to be on total security lockdown.


00:31:58.086 --> 00:32:00.696
Come on, I threatened a terrorist.
Who is that?


00:32:00.697 --> 00:32:05.748
There's only so much I can do, sir, when you give
the world's press your home address.


00:32:16.290 --> 00:32:17.562
Right there's fine.


00:32:21.811 --> 00:32:25.833
You're not the Mandarin, are you?
Are you?


00:32:26.935 --> 00:32:30.795
You don't remember. Why I
am not surprised?


00:32:30.796 --> 00:32:32.460
Don't take it personally, I don't remember
what I had for breakfast.


00:32:32.510 --> 00:32:34.952
- Gluten-free waffles, sir.
- That's right.


00:32:34.967 --> 00:32:39.764
Look, I need to be alone with you, someplace
not here... it's urgent.


00:32:41.673 --> 00:32:45.259
Normally, I'd go for that sort of thing, but now
I'm in a committed relationship


00:32:45.290 --> 00:32:49.368
- It's... with her.
- Tony


00:32:50.351 --> 00:32:53.390
- Is somebody there?
- Yeah, it's Maya Hansen.


00:32:54.485 --> 00:32:58.697
Old botanist pal that I used
to know, barely.


00:32:58.767 --> 00:33:02.169
Please don't tell me that there is a 12-year-old
kid waiting in the car that I've never met.


00:33:02.170 --> 00:33:06.404
- He's 13. No, I need your help.
- What for? Why now?


00:33:06.405 --> 00:33:09.851
Because I read the papers, and, frankly,
I don't think you'll last the week.


00:33:09.852 --> 00:33:11.380
- I'll be fine.
- I'm sorry.


00:33:11.438 --> 00:33:14.659
With Happy in the hospital, I didn't
know we were expecting guests.


00:33:14.660 --> 00:33:15.507
We weren't.


00:33:15.597 --> 00:33:17.362
- And old girlfriends!
- She's not really.


00:33:17.363 --> 00:33:20.192
No, not really. It was
just one night.


00:33:20.198 --> 00:33:23.596
- Yep.
- That's how you did it, isn't it?


00:33:23.597 --> 00:33:24.584
It was a great night


00:33:24.585 --> 00:33:25.842
- Well... you know
- Yeah.


00:33:25.843 --> 00:33:27.720
You have saved yourself
a world of pain.


00:33:27.721 --> 00:33:28.594
- What?
- Trust me.


00:33:28.595 --> 00:33:29.730
We're going out of town.


00:33:29.731 --> 00:33:31.597
- Okay, we've been through this. Nope.
- Yep!


00:33:31.598 --> 00:33:33.998
- The man says no.
- Immediately and indefinitely.


00:33:33.999 --> 00:33:35.593
- Great idea. Let's go.
- I'm sorry.


00:33:35.594 --> 00:33:37.877
That's a terrible idea. Please don't
touch her bags.


00:33:37.878 --> 00:33:39.783
Tony, this is how normal
people behave.


00:33:39.784 --> 00:33:41.915
I can't protect you out there.
I challenged-


00:33:41.916 --> 00:33:43.526
- Is this normal?
- Sadly, that


00:33:43.527 --> 00:33:44.860
Yes, this is normal!


00:33:44.861 --> 00:33:47.710
- Is very normal
- It's a big bunny, relax about it!


00:33:47.711 --> 00:33:50.159
- Calm down!
- I got this for you.


00:33:50.160 --> 00:33:52.489
- I'm aware of that.
- You still haven't even told me that you liked it!


00:33:52.490 --> 00:33:55.019
- I don't like it!
- I asked you three- You don't like it?!


00:33:55.020 --> 00:33:58.392
We are leaving the house, that's not
even up for discussion. - Guys... do we umm...


00:33:58.402 --> 00:34:01.736
- What?
- Do we need to worry about that?


00:34:50.245 --> 00:34:52.909
- I got you.
- I got you first.


00:34:52.929 --> 00:34:54.879
Like I said, we can't
stay here.


00:35:04.009 --> 00:35:06.081
Move! I'm right behind.


00:35:10.903 --> 00:35:12.132
Get her, I'm going to
find a way around.


00:35:12.924 --> 00:35:16.270
Stop stopping! Get her.
Get outside! Go!


00:35:39.471 --> 00:35:41.161
Oh my God.
Tony!


00:35:55.085 --> 00:35:56.905
Sir, Miss Potts is clear
of the structure.


00:36:30.062 --> 00:36:31.742
Jarvis, where's my flight power?


00:36:31.743 --> 00:36:33.767
Working on it, sir. This is
a prototype.


00:36:48.793 --> 00:36:49.870
That's one.


00:36:51.463 --> 00:36:54.547
Sir, the suit is not combat-ready.


00:37:09.599 --> 00:37:11.037
That's two.


00:38:23.820 --> 00:38:25.575
Tony!


00:38:59.740 --> 00:39:02.006
Sir, take a deep breath.


00:39:17.832 --> 00:39:19.395
Flight power restored.


00:39:34.138 --> 00:39:37.080
Sir. Sir!


00:39:37.869 --> 00:39:40.170
Alright, kill the
alarm. I got it.


00:39:40.171 --> 00:39:44.685
That's the emergency alert triggered by
the power dropping below 5%.


00:40:21.422 --> 00:40:24.389
Snow? Where are we,
upstate?


00:40:24.390 --> 00:40:27.044
We are 5 miles outside of
Rose Hills, Tennessee.


00:40:28.010 --> 00:40:29.192
Why?


00:40:29.579 --> 00:40:34.254
Jarvis! Not my idea! What are we
doing here, this is


00:40:34.255 --> 00:40:36.133
thousands of miles away? I've gotta get
Pepper, I've got to -


00:40:37.034 --> 00:40:38.324
I prepared a flight plan.


00:40:38.325 --> 00:40:39.778
This was the location.


00:40:39.832 --> 00:40:42.054
Who asked you? Open
the suit.


00:40:42.055 --> 00:40:44.790
I think I may be malfunctioning, sir.


00:40:44.791 --> 00:40:45.791
Open Eject.


00:40:52.217 --> 00:40:53.296
That's brisk!


00:41:01.427 --> 00:41:03.284
Maybe I'll just cozy back
up for a bit.


00:41:03.285 --> 00:41:06.395
I actually think I need
to sleep now, sir.


00:41:06.470 --> 00:41:07.223
Jarvis.


00:41:09.728 --> 00:41:10.998
Jarvis?


00:41:14.233 --> 00:41:15.503
Don't leave me, buddy.


00:41:37.028 --> 00:41:41.015
Stark Secure Server: Now transferring
to all known receivers.


00:41:41.064 --> 00:41:42.233
Pepper, it's me.


00:41:43.033 --> 00:41:47.328
I've got a lot of apologies to make and not
a lot of time, so first off.


00:41:48.228 --> 00:41:49.837
I'm so sorry I put you
in harm's way.


00:41:49.838 --> 00:41:52.166
That was selfish and stupid and
it won't happen again.


00:41:52.868 --> 00:41:56.626
Also, it's Christmas time. The
rabbit's too big. Done.


00:41:56.646 --> 00:41:58.156
Sorry.


00:41:58.166 --> 00:42:02.690
And I'm sorry in advance because...
I can't come home yet.


00:42:04.234 --> 00:42:07.768
I need to find this guy. You
gotta stay safe.


00:42:07.769 --> 00:42:09.228
That's all I know.


00:42:09.888 --> 00:42:12.495
I just stole a poncho from
a wooden Indian.


00:42:37.027 --> 00:42:38.626
Let's get you comfy.


00:42:40.717 --> 00:42:42.084
You happy now?


00:42:54.077 --> 00:42:55.233
Freeze!


00:42:56.301 --> 00:42:59.500
- Don't move.
- You got me.


00:43:01.881 --> 00:43:03.126
Nice potato gun.


00:43:04.026 --> 00:43:05.369
Barrel's a little long.


00:43:05.370 --> 00:43:09.263
Between that and the wide gauge, it's
going to diminish your FPS.


00:43:13.305 --> 00:43:14.850
And now you're out of ammo.


00:43:15.451 --> 00:43:16.868
What's that thing on
your chest?


00:43:18.282 --> 00:43:22.317
It's a electromagnet. You should know, you've
got a box of them right here.


00:43:22.757 --> 00:43:24.093
What does it power?


00:43:32.947 --> 00:43:34.283
Oh my God!


00:43:39.353 --> 00:43:42.960
- Is that Iron Man?
- Technically, I am.


00:43:42.961 --> 00:43:46.042
Technically, you're dead.


00:43:47.756 --> 00:43:50.502
- A valid point.
- What happened to him?


00:43:50.503 --> 00:43:53.247
Life. I built him. I take
care of him.


00:43:56.164 --> 00:43:58.250
I'll fix him.


00:43:58.251 --> 00:43:59.414
- Like a mechanic.
- Yeah.


00:44:01.870 --> 00:44:04.340
If I was building Iron Man
and War Machine,


00:44:04.341 --> 00:44:06.812
- It's Iron Patriot now.
- That's way cooler!


00:44:06.813 --> 00:44:07.974
No, it's not.


00:44:08.350 --> 00:44:11.949
Anyway, I would have
added in the retro-


00:44:11.950 --> 00:44:14.753
- Retroreflective panels?
- To make him stealth mode.


00:44:14.754 --> 00:44:16.086
- You want a stealth mode?
- Cool, right?


00:44:16.087 --> 00:44:18.615
That's actually a good idea.
Maybe I'll build one.


00:44:19.493 --> 00:44:20.898
Not a good idea!


00:44:20.899 --> 00:44:22.971
What are you doing? You're going
to break his finger?


00:44:22.972 --> 00:44:24.889
He's in pain. He's been injured.
Leave him alone.


00:44:25.210 --> 00:44:26.780
- Sorry.
- Are you?


00:44:28.657 --> 00:44:30.449
Don't worry about it.
I'll fix it.


00:44:31.023 --> 00:44:32.288
So, uh, who's home?


00:44:32.289 --> 00:44:37.348
Well, my mom already left for the diner and
dad went to 7-11 to get scratchers.


00:44:37.734 --> 00:44:40.644
I guess he won 'cause that
was six years ago.


00:44:43.253 --> 00:44:45.826
Which happens, dads leave. No need to
be a pussy about it.


00:44:45.827 --> 00:44:50.355
Here's what I need: a laptop, a
digital watch, a cell phone,


00:44:50.356 --> 00:44:53.446
The pneumatic actuator from
your bazooka over there,


00:44:53.447 --> 00:44:56.312
a map of town, a big spring,
and a tunafish sandwich.


00:44:56.313 --> 00:45:00.224
- What's in it for me?
- Salvation. What's his name?


00:45:00.225 --> 00:45:04.016
- Who?
- The kid that bullies you at school, what's his name?


00:45:04.017 --> 00:45:06.534
How'd you know that?


00:45:06.614 --> 00:45:08.293
I got just the thing.


00:45:10.556 --> 00:45:15.423
This is a pinata for a cricket. I'm kidding.
it's a very powerful weapon.


00:45:15.825 --> 00:45:18.437
Point it away from your face,
press the button on top,


00:45:18.484 --> 00:45:20.176
It discourages bullying.


00:45:20.579 --> 00:45:23.230
Non-lethal, just to cover
one's ass.


00:45:23.301 --> 00:45:28.032
- Deal. Deal? What'd you say?
- Deal.


00:45:28.820 --> 00:45:31.335
- What's your name?
- Harley


00:45:31.336 --> 00:45:32.486
Tony


00:45:34.697 --> 00:45:36.549
You know what keeps going
through my head?


00:45:37.149 --> 00:45:38.790
Where's my sandwich?


00:46:16.905 --> 00:46:20.146
Stark Secure Server. Retinal
scan verified.


00:46:20.442 --> 00:46:21.527
Pepper, it's me.


00:46:21.818 --> 00:46:23.603
I've got a lot of apologies
to make


00:46:23.604 --> 00:46:25.338
and not a lot of time,
so first off.


00:46:25.677 --> 00:46:27.616
I'm so sorry I put you
in harm's way.


00:46:27.617 --> 00:46:30.371
That was selfish and stupid and
it won't happen again.


00:46:32.638 --> 00:46:34.969
Why were you at the
house tonight?


00:46:34.970 --> 00:46:38.431
What was so important that you
had to speak to Tony?


00:46:41.299 --> 00:46:44.006
I think that my boss is working
for the Mandarin.


00:46:45.843 --> 00:46:47.526
So if you still want
to talk about it,


00:46:47.527 --> 00:46:49.709
I suggest we get ourselves
someplace safe.


00:46:51.399 --> 00:46:54.213
Your boss works for the
Mandarin you think,


00:46:54.214 --> 00:46:57.104
but Tony says you're a botanist.


00:46:57.105 --> 00:47:00.595
That figures. What I actually am is a biological
DNA coder running a team of


00:47:00.596 --> 00:47:04.132
40 out of a privately-funded think tank, but
sure you can call me a "botanist".


00:47:06.530 --> 00:47:09.489
This boss of yours, does
he have a name?


00:47:09.490 --> 00:47:11.077
Yeah, Aldrich Killian.


00:47:13.886 --> 00:47:16.931
Well we took the house down sir, but
there's no sign of a body.


00:47:17.131 --> 00:47:18.543
- I see.
- No Stark.


00:47:18.643 --> 00:47:19.817
I have to go.


00:47:20.652 --> 00:47:23.075
The Master is about to record
and he's a little...


00:47:24.275 --> 00:47:25.622
Well you know how he gets.


00:47:25.698 --> 00:47:28.616
Keep your appointment tonight and
call me when it's done.


00:47:34.505 --> 00:47:37.103
Alright everybody. No talking and
no eye contact,


00:47:37.104 --> 00:47:39.077
unless you wanna get
shot in the face.


00:47:59.831 --> 00:48:01.498
The Master is travelling.


00:48:16.183 --> 00:48:18.182
Well then, what are we waiting for?


00:48:21.037 --> 00:48:23.283
The sandwich was fair, the
spring was a little


00:48:23.284 --> 00:48:25.434
rusty, the rest of the materials
I'll make do.


00:48:26.256 --> 00:48:28.799
By the way, when you said your
sister had a watch, I


00:48:28.800 --> 00:48:31.091
was kinda hoping for something
a little more than that.


00:48:31.566 --> 00:48:34.793
She's six! Anyway, it's limited edition.


00:48:35.392 --> 00:48:38.979
- When can we talk about New York?
- Maybe never, relax about it.


00:48:38.980 --> 00:48:40.547
- What about the Avengers, can you talk about them?
- I don't know. later.


00:48:40.548 --> 00:48:41.778
Hey kid, give me more space.


00:48:46.443 --> 00:48:50.102
What's the official story here?
What happened?


00:48:50.327 --> 00:48:54.261
I guess this guy named Chad Davis,
used to live roundabouts.


00:48:55.859 --> 00:48:58.052
Won a bunch of medals in the army.


00:48:58.289 --> 00:49:02.343
One day, folks said he went crazy
and made, you know, a bomb.


00:49:02.938 --> 00:49:05.863
Then he blew himself
up right here.


00:49:11.533 --> 00:49:13.780
- Six people died, right?
- Yes.


00:49:13.781 --> 00:49:15.430
- Including Chad Davis?
- Yea.


00:49:23.928 --> 00:49:25.261
Doesn't make sense.


00:49:26.211 --> 00:49:29.454
Think about it. Six dead,
only five shadows.


00:49:29.537 --> 00:49:34.779
Yeah, but people said these shadows are
like the mark of souls gone to Heaven


00:49:35.342 --> 00:49:40.782
Except the bomb guy, he went to Hell on
account of he didn't get a shadow.


00:49:41.136 --> 00:49:44.285
- That's why there's only five.
- Do you buy that?


00:49:44.286 --> 00:49:45.885
That's what everyone says.


00:49:49.122 --> 00:49:51.858
You know what this crater
reminds me of?


00:49:51.859 --> 00:49:53.894
I have no idea. I don't care.


00:49:55.316 --> 00:50:00.674
That giant wormhole, in
um, in New York.


00:50:00.680 --> 00:50:02.021
Does it remind you?


00:50:02.822 --> 00:50:04.745
That's manipulative. I don't want
to talk about it.


00:50:04.746 --> 00:50:07.191
Are they coming back?
The aliens?


00:50:07.192 --> 00:50:08.753
Maybe, can you stop?


00:50:10.007 --> 00:50:12.134
Remember when I told you that
I have an anxiety issue?


00:50:12.135 --> 00:50:14.203
Does this subject make
you edgy?


00:50:14.204 --> 00:50:14.725
Yeah, a little bit.


00:50:14.726 --> 00:50:16.976
Can I just catch my breath
for a second?


00:50:16.977 --> 00:50:21.014
Are there bad guys in Rose Hills? Do you need
a plastic bag to breathe into?


00:50:21.079 --> 00:50:22.650
- Do you have medication?
- Nope.


00:50:22.935 --> 00:50:24.272
- Do you need to be on it?
- Probably.


00:50:24.273 --> 00:50:26.310
- Do you have PTSD?
- I don't think so.


00:50:26.311 --> 00:50:28.026
Are you going completely
mental?


00:50:28.027 --> 00:50:30.011
I can stop, do you want
me to stop?


00:50:30.012 --> 00:50:31.776
Remember when I said
to stop doing that?


00:50:31.777 --> 00:50:33.714
I swear to God, you're going
to freak me out.


00:50:35.756 --> 00:50:37.814
Ah man, you did it, didn't you?


00:50:37.815 --> 00:50:40.069
- You happy now?
- What did I say?


00:50:40.070 --> 00:50:44.383
Hey, wait up!
Wait, wait.


00:50:49.443 --> 00:50:51.161
What the hell was that?


00:50:55.054 --> 00:50:57.517
Your fault, you spazzed
me out.


00:50:59.082 --> 00:51:01.087
Okay, back to business.
Where were we?


00:51:01.613 --> 00:51:06.391
The guy who died... relatives?Mom?
Ms. Davis, where is she?


00:51:06.399 --> 00:51:09.400
- Where she always is.
- See, now you're being helpful.


00:51:15.165 --> 00:51:20.207
Sorry. Lady, this uh,


00:51:21.608 --> 00:51:23.218
Thank you.


00:51:25.541 --> 00:51:26.842
Nice haircut, suits you.


00:51:28.611 --> 00:51:31.114
- Nice watch.
- Yeah, limited edition.


00:51:31.514 --> 00:51:33.002
Oh, I don't doubt it.


00:51:34.659 --> 00:51:36.318
Well have a good evening.


00:51:59.418 --> 00:52:03.255
Ms. Davis, Mind if
I join you?


00:52:03.312 --> 00:52:05.863
- Free country.
- It sure is.


00:52:10.866 --> 00:52:11.989
Alright


00:52:13.933 --> 00:52:18.204
- Where'd you like to start?
- I just want to say I'm sorry about your loss.


00:52:18.757 --> 00:52:20.791
I want to know what you
think happened


00:52:24.490 --> 00:52:28.695
I brought your damn file.
You take it and go.


00:52:28.830 --> 00:52:31.920
Whatever was in here, he
wanted no part of it.


00:52:33.451 --> 00:52:37.397
Clearly, you were waiting for someone else.
Supposed to meet somebody here?


00:52:38.398 --> 00:52:39.408
Yeah.


00:52:52.759 --> 00:52:56.327
Ms. Davis, your son didn't kill
himself. I guarantee


00:52:56.328 --> 00:53:00.318
you he didn't kill anyone.
Someone used him.


00:53:01.366 --> 00:53:04.633
- What?
- As a weapon.


00:53:08.424 --> 00:53:11.889
You're not the person who called
me after all, are you?


00:53:13.230 --> 00:53:14.844
Actually, I am.


00:53:17.919 --> 00:53:21.718
Hey, hey! What's all this about?
The hell's going on here?


00:53:21.719 --> 00:53:23.427
It's called an arrest.


00:53:24.807 --> 00:53:27.540
- Sheriff, is it?
- Yes ma'am, it is. And you are?


00:53:27.541 --> 00:53:31.984
- Homeland Security. We good here?
- No, we're not good.


00:53:31.985 --> 00:53:35.987
- I need a little more information than that.
- Well, I think it's a little above your pay grade, Sheriff.


00:53:35.988 --> 00:53:40.289
Yeah, well, why don't you get on the
horn to Nashville and upgrade me?


00:53:40.290 --> 00:53:43.351
Alright, you know what, I was hoping
to do this the smart way, but uh,


00:53:43.471 --> 00:53:45.632
The fun way's always good.


00:53:46.833 --> 00:53:48.034
Deputy, get this woman and-


00:54:02.122 --> 00:54:04.842
Hey hot wings, you wanna party?
You and me, let's go.


00:54:17.876 --> 00:54:19.979
- Crazy, huh?
- Yeah.


00:54:21.999 --> 00:54:22.740
Watch this.


00:55:28.678 --> 00:55:31.520
You walked right into this one. I've dated
hotter chicks than you.


00:55:33.561 --> 00:55:37.804
That's all you got? Cheap trick
and a cheesy one-liner?


00:55:37.805 --> 00:55:40.166
Sweetheart, that could be the name
of my autobiography.


00:56:42.201 --> 00:56:44.242
- Let me go!
- Help me! Help me!


00:56:50.447 --> 00:56:52.928
Hey kid, what would you
like for Christmas?


00:56:52.929 --> 00:56:54.629
Mr. Stark, I am so sorry.


00:56:54.630 --> 00:56:57.770
No, no, I think he was trying to say
"I want my goddamn file."


00:56:58.092 --> 00:57:00.053
It's not your fault kid.


00:57:02.253 --> 00:57:03.994
Remember what I told you
about bullies?


00:57:09.817 --> 00:57:13.219
You like that, West World? That's
the thing about smart guys.


00:57:13.779 --> 00:57:15.901
We always cover our ass.


00:57:40.074 --> 00:57:41.955
You're welcome!


00:57:43.237 --> 00:57:46.699
- For what? Did I miss something?
- Me saving your life.


00:57:46.799 --> 00:57:49.300
A: Saved you first
B: Thanks, sort of


00:57:49.842 --> 00:57:52.462
And C: If you do someone a solid, don't
be a yutz alright,


00:57:52.463 --> 00:57:54.984
just play it cool otherwise you
come off grandiose.


00:57:56.685 --> 00:57:58.326
Unlike you?


00:57:59.447 --> 00:58:02.589
Admit it: you need me.
We're connected.


00:58:02.728 --> 00:58:04.990
What I need is for you to go home,
be with your mom,


00:58:04.991 --> 00:58:07.851
keep your trap shut, and
guard the suit.


00:58:07.852 --> 00:58:09.567
And stay connected to the
telephone because


00:58:09.568 --> 00:58:10.872
if I call you better
pick up. Okay?


00:58:10.873 --> 00:58:13.574
Can you feel that?
We're done here.


00:58:14.036 --> 00:58:16.677
Move out of the way or I'm going to
run you over. Bye kid.


00:58:23.786 --> 00:58:27.348
I'm sorry kid. You
did good.


00:58:27.349 --> 00:58:30.649
So now you're just going to leave
you here, like my dad?


00:58:31.665 --> 00:58:35.892
Yeah. Wait, you're guilt-tripping
me, aren't you?


00:58:35.893 --> 00:58:37.649
I'm cold


00:58:37.990 --> 00:58:40.731
I can tell. You know how I can tell?


00:58:41.151 --> 00:58:42.492
'Cause we're connected.


00:58:46.795 --> 00:58:48.875
It was worth a shot.


00:59:06.807 --> 00:59:08.747
What happened to the picture?


00:59:18.212 --> 00:59:20.734
The entire East coast.. the
satellites are down.


00:59:23.115 --> 00:59:24.597
We have an unauthorized broadcast


00:59:25.127 --> 00:59:27.171
Mr. Vice President, I think
you should see this.


00:59:29.891 --> 00:59:31.742
Oh my God, not again.


00:59:32.944 --> 00:59:34.974
Is the President getting this?


00:59:45.494 --> 00:59:47.395
Mr. President.


00:59:47.696 --> 00:59:49.496
Only two lessons remain.


00:59:50.178 --> 00:59:52.978
I intend to finish this before
Christmas morning.


00:59:54.220 --> 00:59:58.662
Meet Thomas Richards. Good strong
name, good strong job.


01:00:00.023 --> 01:00:04.626
Thomas here is an accountant for
the Roxxon Oil Corporation.


01:00:08.027 --> 01:00:09.950
And I'm sure he's a
really good guy.


01:00:13.191 --> 01:00:17.993
I'm going to shoot him in the head, live on
your television, in 30 seconds.


01:00:18.875 --> 01:00:23.477
The number for this telephone is in your
cell phone. Exciting, isn't it?


01:00:23.757 --> 01:00:25.838
Imagining how it got there.


01:00:26.037 --> 01:00:32.262
America, if your president calls me in
the next half-minute, Tom lives.


01:00:32.562 --> 01:00:33.522
Go.


01:00:35.805 --> 01:00:37.059
How did he hack my phone?


01:00:37.060 --> 01:00:38.966
We can't allow terrorists
to dictate


01:00:38.967 --> 01:00:40.173
I have to make this call.


01:00:40.174 --> 01:00:41.767
I'd strongly advise
against that.


01:00:41.768 --> 01:00:43.368
This is the right
thing to do.


01:01:11.264 --> 01:01:13.737
There's just one lesson left,
President Ellis,


01:01:13.738 --> 01:01:15.946
so run away and kiss your
children goodbye


01:01:15.947 --> 01:01:18.084
Because nothing, not your army,
not your red,


01:01:18.085 --> 01:01:19.990
white, and blue attack dog,
can save you.


01:01:23.632 --> 01:01:24.832
I'll see you soon.


01:01:27.674 --> 01:01:30.485
Tell Rhodes, find this lunatic
right now.


01:01:30.486 --> 01:01:33.157
Sir, we tracked the broadcast signal.


01:01:33.158 --> 01:01:36.076
We have a possible point of origin in Pakistan
and the Patriot is ready to strike.


01:01:36.077 --> 01:01:36.920
- Right now!
- Yes, sir.


01:02:08.579 --> 01:02:09.538
Don't move!


01:02:16.743 --> 01:02:17.744
Uh, hang on a second.


01:02:18.784 --> 01:02:19.496
Hello.


01:02:19.497 --> 01:02:24.745
You ever look up and everything starts glowing from
the inside out, a kind of bright orange.


01:02:25.347 --> 01:02:27.790
- Yeah, I've had that. Who is this?
- It's me, pal.


01:02:27.791 --> 01:02:30.991
Now last time I went missing, if I remember
correctly, you went looking for me.


01:02:30.992 --> 01:02:34.109
- What are you doing?
- A little talking, making friends in Pakistan.


01:02:34.110 --> 01:02:35.415
What are you doing?


01:02:35.416 --> 01:02:38.796
Your re-design, your big re-brand,
that was AIM, right? - Yeah.


01:02:39.396 --> 01:02:43.078
I'm gonna find a heavy-duty comsat
right now, I need your login.


01:02:43.418 --> 01:02:45.257
Same as it's always been,
War Machine 68.


01:02:45.258 --> 01:02:46.220
And password please?


01:02:46.320 --> 01:02:48.807
Well, look, I gotta change it every time
you hack in, Tony.


01:02:48.808 --> 01:02:51.842
It's not the eighties, nobody says "hack"
anymore, give me your login.


01:02:53.364 --> 01:02:56.426
"War Machine Rox" with
an X, all caps.


01:02:59.928 --> 01:03:04.130
- Yeah okay.
- That is so much better than Iron Patriot.


01:03:45.540 --> 01:03:47.782
That ain't gonna cut it.


01:03:50.463 --> 01:03:52.625
Excuse me sir, I don't know who...


01:03:55.346 --> 01:03:58.028
Mom, I need to call you back. Something
magical is happening.


01:03:58.748 --> 01:04:00.685
- Tony Stark is in my van.
- Keep it down.


01:04:00.686 --> 01:04:02.670
- Tony Stark is in my van!
- No, he's not.


01:04:02.671 --> 01:04:04.066
I knew you were still alive!


01:04:04.067 --> 01:04:05.712
Come on in and close the door.


01:04:10.755 --> 01:04:12.317
- Wow, can I just say sir?
- Yeah.


01:04:13.637 --> 01:04:14.582
I am your biggest fan.


01:04:14.583 --> 01:04:17.120
First, is this your van or
is anyone else gonna come in?


01:04:17.121 --> 01:04:18.309
No, no, it's just us.


01:04:18.310 --> 01:04:19.440
What's your name?


01:04:19.441 --> 01:04:20.635
- Gary.
- Gary.


01:04:21.861 --> 01:04:22.961
Oh wow.


01:04:22.962 --> 01:04:27.004
Right there's fine. I get a
lot of this, it's okay.


01:04:27.005 --> 01:04:28.324
Can I just say?


01:04:28.325 --> 01:04:32.089
- Yeah.
- I don't know if you can tell but I have like


01:04:32.609 --> 01:04:35.593
Patterned my whole look after you. My
hair's a little,


01:04:35.594 --> 01:04:38.251
it's not right because there's
some product in it.


01:04:38.252 --> 01:04:38.411
Right.


01:04:40.172 --> 01:04:42.487
I don't want to make things
awkward for you


01:04:42.488 --> 01:04:44.695
- No.
- But I do have to show you... boom!


01:04:45.937 --> 01:04:47.437
Hispanic Scott Baio?


01:04:48.577 --> 01:04:50.138
- Oh, I'm sorry, is that me?
- Yeah.


01:04:50.538 --> 01:04:53.437
It's... I mean. I had them do it
off a doll that I made,


01:04:53.438 --> 01:04:56.662
so it's not like it's off a picture. So
it's a little bit-


01:04:56.663 --> 01:04:59.183
Jerry, for a moment, listen
to me here.


01:04:59.904 --> 01:05:01.853
I don't want to clip your
wings here.


01:05:01.854 --> 01:05:03.546
We're both a little over-excited.


01:05:03.866 --> 01:05:06.389
I have an issue. I'm chasing bad
guys, trying to grapple


01:05:06.390 --> 01:05:08.469
with something from some
hard-crypt data files.


01:05:08.470 --> 01:05:10.090
I don't have enough juice.


01:05:10.150 --> 01:05:13.951
I need you to jump on the roof,
recalibrate the ISDNs


01:05:14.552 --> 01:05:17.688
- Pump it up by about 40%.
- Got it.


01:05:17.689 --> 01:05:18.475
Alright, it's a mission.


01:05:18.500 --> 01:05:19.274
Yeah.


01:05:19.275 --> 01:05:20.937
Tony needs Gary.


01:05:21.437 --> 01:05:22.387
And Gary needs Tony.


01:05:22.388 --> 01:05:23.437
Be quiet about it.


01:05:23.638 --> 01:05:24.738
Go.


01:05:47.332 --> 01:05:50.254
What would you regard as the defining
moment of your life?


01:05:50.573 --> 01:05:54.216
Well uh, I think that would be the day I decided
not to let my injury beat me.


01:05:56.577 --> 01:05:59.500
- Can you please state your name for the camera?
- Ellen Brandt.


01:05:59.819 --> 01:06:04.182
Okay, so, the injections are
administered periodically.


01:06:04.183 --> 01:06:08.665
Addiction will not be tolerated and those who cannot
regulate will be cut from the program.


01:06:09.866 --> 01:06:16.950
Once misfits, cripples... you are the next
iteration of human evolution.


01:06:21.232 --> 01:06:25.163
Hi everybody. Before we start, I promise you, looking back
at your life there will be


01:06:25.164 --> 01:06:29.276
nothing as bitter as the memory of that glorious risk that
you prudently elected to forego.


01:06:30.777 --> 01:06:32.999
Today is your glory. Let's begin!


01:06:44.325 --> 01:06:47.207
We gotta get out of here! Gotta get out of here!
Get 'em out! Get 'em out of here!


01:06:54.211 --> 01:06:56.573
A bomb is not a bomb
when it's a misfire.


01:06:59.013 --> 01:07:01.295
This stuff doesn't always
work, right, pal?


01:07:01.695 --> 01:07:03.796
It's faulty, but you found a
buyer, didn't ya?


01:07:04.338 --> 01:07:06.358
Sold it to the Mandarin.


01:07:11.901 --> 01:07:15.222
What happened? Fun fact.


01:07:16.225 --> 01:07:18.986
Before he built rockets
for the Nazis.


01:07:19.345 --> 01:07:28.310
The idealistic Werner von Braun dreamed
of space travel... he stargazed.


01:07:29.351 --> 01:07:33.313
You know what he said when the
first V2 hit London?


01:07:34.034 --> 01:07:37.356
The rocket performed perfectly.


01:07:39.158 --> 01:07:41.439
It just landed on the wrong planet.


01:07:43.159 --> 01:07:48.042
See we all begin wide-eyed...
"pure science".


01:07:48.562 --> 01:07:52.805
Then the ego steps in,
the obsession


01:07:54.366 --> 01:08:00.608
And when you look up, you're
a long way from shore.


01:08:01.370 --> 01:08:07.774
You can't be too hard on yourself, Maya. I mean
you gave your research to a think tank.


01:08:07.775 --> 01:08:11.207
Yeah but Killian built that think tank
on military contracts.


01:08:11.208 --> 01:08:13.177
That's exactly what we used to do.


01:08:13.738 --> 01:08:15.299
So don't judge yourself.


01:08:17.259 --> 01:08:18.739
Thank you, Pepper.


01:08:20.661 --> 01:08:22.182
I really appreciate that.


01:08:30.067 --> 01:08:30.582
Hi, good evening


01:08:30.583 --> 01:08:31.848
- Good evening.
- Come on in.


01:08:34.228 --> 01:08:35.390
Maya, run!


01:08:37.711 --> 01:08:38.832
Hi Pepper.


01:08:41.073 --> 01:08:43.273
So you want to tell me why you were
at Stark's manison last night?


01:08:43.354 --> 01:08:46.755
I'm trying to fix this thing. I didn't know you and
the Master were gonna blow the place up.


01:08:47.277 --> 01:08:51.257
Oh I see, so you were trying to save Stark...
when he threatened us


01:08:51.258 --> 01:08:52.681
I told you, Killian, we can use him.


01:08:54.521 --> 01:08:55.805
Pepper, Pepper, Pepper


01:08:55.806 --> 01:08:59.365
Look if we want to launch product
next year, I need Stark.


01:08:59.725 --> 01:09:02.824
He just lacked a decent incentive.
Now he has one.


01:09:07.596 --> 01:09:12.829
This is Support Team Blue 0, sending coordinates for
suspected Mandarin broadcast point of origin.


01:09:12.830 --> 01:09:13.405
Copy.


01:09:21.738 --> 01:09:22.817
Nobody move!


01:09:27.741 --> 01:09:30.848
Support Blue 0, unless the Mandarin's
next attack on the U.S.


01:09:30.849 --> 01:09:33.904
involves cheaply-made sportswear, I think
you messed up again.


01:09:35.425 --> 01:09:40.387
Yes, you're free, if you weren't
before. Yes ma'am.


01:09:40.588 --> 01:09:44.350
Iron Patriot on the job, happy to help,no need
to thank me, it's my pleasure.


01:09:53.396 --> 01:09:55.898
Savin, I've acquired the Patriot armor.


01:09:55.899 --> 01:09:59.839
You want this suit? You're going ot have
to pry my cold, dead body out of it.


01:09:59.840 --> 01:10:01.320
That's the plan, Colonel.


01:10:02.960 --> 01:10:05.216
Harley, tell me what is happening,
give me a full report.


01:10:05.317 --> 01:10:08.924
Yeah, I'm still eating that candy, do you
want me to keep eating it?


01:10:09.325 --> 01:10:10.325
How much did you have?


01:10:10.326 --> 01:10:11.326
Two or three bowls.


01:10:11.327 --> 01:10:13.631
- Can you still see straight?
- Sort of.


01:10:13.632 --> 01:10:15.607
That means you're fine,
give me Jarvis.


01:10:16.049 --> 01:10:17.110
Jarvis, how are we?


01:10:17.111 --> 01:10:19.536
It's totally fine sir. I seem to do quite
well for a stretch and


01:10:19.537 --> 01:10:21.732
then at the end of the sentence I
say the wrong cranberry.


01:10:22.112 --> 01:10:25.459
And sir, you were right. Once I factored
in available AIM downlink


01:10:25.460 --> 01:10:28.756
facilities I was able to pinpoint the
Mandarin's broadcast signal.


01:10:29.456 --> 01:10:33.559
What're we talkin'? The Far East, Europe, North
Africa, Iran, Pakistan, Syria, where is it?


01:10:33.859 --> 01:10:35.180
Actually, sir, it's in Miami.


01:10:35.181 --> 01:10:38.791
Okay, kid, I'm going to have to walk
you through rebooting Jarvis's


01:10:38.792 --> 01:10:40.923
speech drive, but not right now.


01:10:41.348 --> 01:10:42.423
Harley, where is he really?


01:10:42.424 --> 01:10:44.105
Just look on the screen and
tell me where it is.


01:10:45.866 --> 01:10:47.311
Um...it does say Miami, Florida.


01:10:47.312 --> 01:10:49.868
Okay, first things first,
I need the armor.


01:10:50.108 --> 01:10:51.382
Where are we at with it?


01:10:51.383 --> 01:10:52.550
Uh, it's not charging.


01:10:59.474 --> 01:11:03.259
Actually, sir, it is charging, but the power
source is questionable.


01:11:03.560 --> 01:11:05.798
It may not succeed in revitalizing
the Mark 42.


01:11:05.799 --> 01:11:08.088
What's questionable about electricity?


01:11:08.089 --> 01:11:11.201
Alright, it's my suit and I can't...
I'm not gonna...


01:11:12.241 --> 01:11:15.603
- Oh God, not again.
- Tony


01:11:17.565 --> 01:11:20.786
Are you having another attack? I didn't even
mention New York.


01:11:20.787 --> 01:11:24.569
Right, and then you just said it, by name,
while denying having said it.


01:11:24.570 --> 01:11:25.749
Okay, um, uh


01:11:28.492 --> 01:11:30.104
Oh God, what am I gonna do?


01:11:30.105 --> 01:11:32.253
Just breathe, really just breathe.


01:11:33.454 --> 01:11:36.976
- You're a mechanic, right?
- Right.


01:11:38.176 --> 01:11:41.537
- You said so.
- Yes, I did.


01:11:42.498 --> 01:11:44.540
What don't you just build something?


01:11:57.348 --> 01:12:00.149
Okay, thanks kid.


01:13:44.170 --> 01:13:48.413
Why is it so hot in here? I told
you to put it at 68.


01:13:49.213 --> 01:13:53.015
My fault again...let me tell you something
sweetheart, I am not your personal-


01:14:56.132 --> 01:14:58.014
I wouldn't go in there for twenty minutes!


01:14:59.434 --> 01:15:02.656
- Now, which one of you is Vanessa?
- That's me.


01:15:02.669 --> 01:15:04.871
Ah, Nessie.


01:15:05.157 --> 01:15:09.743
Did you know that fortune cookies
aren't even Chinese?


01:15:09.744 --> 01:15:12.161
There's some guy over here.


01:15:12.162 --> 01:15:15.584
They're made by Americans, based
on the Japanese recipes. - Hey!


01:15:17.711 --> 01:15:19.712
Bloody hell. Bloody hell.


01:15:19.737 --> 01:15:21.338
- Don't move.
- I am not moving.


01:15:21.347 --> 01:15:24.033
If you want something, take it, although
the guns are all fake


01:15:24.034 --> 01:15:26.550
because those wankers wouldn't trust
me with the real ones.


01:15:26.551 --> 01:15:28.931
- What?
- Hey, do you fancy either of the birds?


01:15:29.492 --> 01:15:34.034
Heard enough. You're not him, the Mandarin,
the real guy, where?


01:15:35.035 --> 01:15:39.357
- Where's the Mandarin? Where is he?
- He's here. He's here.


01:15:39.577 --> 01:15:42.379
- But he's not here. He's here but he's not here.
- What do you mean?


01:15:42.479 --> 01:15:44.866
It's complicated, hey, it's
complicated, alright?


01:15:44.867 --> 01:15:46.201
- It is?
- It's complicated.


01:15:46.202 --> 01:15:47.746
Uncomplicate it. Ladies out, get out
of the bed


01:15:47.747 --> 01:15:49.082
get in the bathroom.


01:15:51.833 --> 01:15:52.442
Sit.


01:16:02.290 --> 01:16:05.474
My name is Trevor, Trevor Slattery.


01:16:05.475 --> 01:16:06.814
What are you?


01:16:07.974 --> 01:16:10.001
What're you a decoy? You're
a double, right?


01:16:10.002 --> 01:16:11.856
What? No. An understudy?
Absolutely not.


01:16:12.617 --> 01:16:14.458
Don't hurt me please!
I'm an actor.


01:16:15.557 --> 01:16:18.311
You got a minute to live, fill it
with words.


01:16:19.012 --> 01:16:22.303
It's just a role. "The Mandarin", see,
it's not real.


01:16:22.623 --> 01:16:24.223
Then how did you get here,
Trevor?


01:16:26.905 --> 01:16:32.530
Um, well, uh, I have a little problem
with, um, substances,


01:16:32.531 --> 01:16:37.311
and I ended up doing things...
no two ways about it


01:16:37.312 --> 01:16:40.593
- In the street that a man shouldn't do.
- Next!


01:16:40.594 --> 01:16:45.996
Then, they approached me about the role
and they knew about the drugs.


01:16:45.997 --> 01:16:47.613
What'd they say they'd get
you off them?


01:16:47.614 --> 01:16:48.638
Said they'd give me more.


01:16:48.998 --> 01:16:52.062
They gave me things. They gave
me this palace.


01:16:52.063 --> 01:16:55.322
They gave me plastic surgery. They
gave me things.


01:16:57.043 --> 01:16:58.443
Did you just nod off?


01:16:59.604 --> 01:17:03.687
No, the lovely speedboat! And the
thing was, he needed someone.


01:17:04.088 --> 01:17:07.690
To take credit for some
"accidental explosions".


01:17:11.250 --> 01:17:12.091
"He"?


01:17:14.732 --> 01:17:16.934
- Killian?
- Killian.


01:17:16.935 --> 01:17:19.257
- He created you?
- He created me.


01:17:20.457 --> 01:17:22.658
- Custom-made terror threat
- Yes!


01:17:23.338 --> 01:17:28.261
Yes, his think tank thinked it up, the
pathology of the serial killer.


01:17:28.701 --> 01:17:31.743
The manipulation of Western
iconography.


01:17:32.183 --> 01:17:36.387
Ready for another lesson?
Blah blah blah.


01:17:38.187 --> 01:17:41.147
Of course, it was my performance that
brought the Mandarin to life.


01:17:41.369 --> 01:17:46.712
Your performance? Where
people die?


01:17:47.672 --> 01:17:50.174
No, no, look around you,
costumes, green screen.


01:17:50.474 --> 01:17:54.716
Honestly, I wasn't on location for half this stuff,
and when I was, movie magic, love.


01:17:54.956 --> 01:17:58.398
I'm sorry but I got a best friend who's in
a coma and he might not wake up.


01:17:58.399 --> 01:18:01.881
So you're going to have to answer for that.
You're still going down, pal.


01:18:08.263 --> 01:18:11.066
Okay, Trevor, what'd you tell him?


01:18:11.767 --> 01:18:13.847
- I didn't tell him anything.
- Nothing?


01:18:15.368 --> 01:18:18.090
- No.
- You should have pressed the panic button.


01:18:18.930 --> 01:18:20.972
Well I panicked, but then
I handled it.


01:18:43.394 --> 01:18:45.114
Just like old times, huh?


01:18:45.115 --> 01:18:47.796
Oh yeah, with zip-ties.
It's a ball.


01:18:48.076 --> 01:18:49.340
It wasn't my idea.


01:18:49.341 --> 01:18:51.799
Okay, so you took
Killian's card


01:18:51.800 --> 01:18:52.749
I took his money.


01:18:52.850 --> 01:18:55.561
And here you are 13 years
later in a dungeon.


01:18:55.761 --> 01:18:56.642
- No.
- Yeah.


01:18:56.742 --> 01:19:00.764
- No, you're in a dungeon. I'm free to go.
- Yeah...


01:19:04.646 --> 01:19:08.999
A lot's happened Tony,
and I'm close.


01:19:09.289 --> 01:19:12.350
Extremis is pratically stable.


01:19:12.351 --> 01:19:12.690
I'm telling you it isn't.


01:19:12.691 --> 01:19:17.354
I saw him on the street, people are going 'bang', they're
painting the walls. Maya, you're kidding yourself.


01:19:17.355 --> 01:19:20.235
Then help me fix it.


01:19:24.259 --> 01:19:25.260
Did I do that?


01:19:27.421 --> 01:19:29.823
- Yes.
- I remember the night, not the morning


01:19:30.544 --> 01:19:31.724
Is this what you've been
chasing around?


01:19:31.725 --> 01:19:32.904
- You don't remember?
- I can't help you.


01:19:35.026 --> 01:19:40.229
You used to have a moral psychology.
You used to have ideals.


01:19:41.149 --> 01:19:44.992
Wanted to help people, now
look at you.


01:19:46.593 --> 01:19:48.814
I get to wake up every morning
with someone who...


01:19:51.541 --> 01:19:52.741
still has a soul.


01:19:59.121 --> 01:20:03.723
Get me out of here,
come on.


01:20:05.564 --> 01:20:10.647
You know what my old man used to say to me?
His favorite of many sayings.


01:20:11.607 --> 01:20:16.129
"The early bird gets the worm, the second
mouse gets the cheese".


01:20:16.130 --> 01:20:18.743
You're not still pissed about the Switzerland
thing, are you?


01:20:18.744 --> 01:20:20.092
How can I be pissed you, Tony?


01:20:20.812 --> 01:20:22.983
I'm here to thank you. You've
given me the


01:20:22.984 --> 01:20:25.255
greatest gift that anybody's
ever given me.


01:20:25.615 --> 01:20:29.027
Desperation. If you think
back to Switzerland,


01:20:29.028 --> 01:20:31.779
you said you'd meet me on
the rooftop, right?


01:20:32.560 --> 01:20:37.893
Well for the first 20 minutes, I actually
thought you'd show up.


01:20:38.194 --> 01:20:40.243
For the next hour, I uhh...


01:20:40.843 --> 01:20:47.508
Well I considered taking that one step shortcut
to the lobby, if you know I mean.


01:20:47.509 --> 01:20:50.431
Honestly, I'm still trying to figure out
what happened to the first mouse.


01:20:50.470 --> 01:20:54.246
But as I looked out over that city, nobody
knew I was there,


01:20:54.347 --> 01:20:56.974
nobody could see me, no one
was even looking.


01:20:57.174 --> 01:21:02.318
I had a thought that would guide
me for years to come.


01:21:03.237 --> 01:21:04.558
Anonymity, Tony.


01:21:06.039 --> 01:21:09.223
Thanks to you, it's been my mantra
ever since, right?


01:21:09.224 --> 01:21:11.522
You simply rule from behind
the scenes.


01:21:11.523 --> 01:21:13.844
Because the second you
give evil a face


01:21:14.004 --> 01:21:17.666
Bin Laden, Gaddafi, The Mandarin


01:21:17.847 --> 01:21:18.989
You hand the people a target.


01:21:18.990 --> 01:21:19.967
You're something else.


01:21:23.012 --> 01:21:24.289
You have met him, I assume?


01:21:24.290 --> 01:21:25.613
Yeah, Sir Lawrence Oblivion.


01:21:25.894 --> 01:21:29.056
I know he's a little over the top sometimes...
it's not entirely my fault.


01:21:29.057 --> 01:21:31.218
He has a tend...he's
a stage actor.


01:21:32.017 --> 01:21:34.579
They say his Lear was the toast of
Croydon, wherever that is.


01:21:35.179 --> 01:21:39.581
Anyway, the point is ever since that big dude
with the hammer fell out of the sky.


01:21:40.462 --> 01:21:42.264
Subtlety's kinda had its day.


01:21:42.583 --> 01:21:44.144
What's next for you in your world?


01:21:44.145 --> 01:21:48.988
Well, I wanted to repay you for the same gift
you so graciously imparted to me.


01:21:56.471 --> 01:22:01.313
Desperation. Now, this is live. I'm not
sure if you can tell.


01:22:01.835 --> 01:22:07.558
But at this moment the body is trying to decide
whether to accept Extremis or just give up.


01:22:07.617 --> 01:22:13.239
And if it gives up, I have to say the denotation
is quite spectactular.


01:22:15.122 --> 01:22:17.844
But until that point, it's really
just a lot of pain.


01:22:18.563 --> 01:22:22.247
We haven't even talked
salary yet.


01:22:23.047 --> 01:22:25.932
What kind of perk package
are you thinking of?


01:22:26.033 --> 01:22:27.170
Let him go.


01:22:28.929 --> 01:22:34.093
- Hold on, hold on. Maya
- I said let him go!


01:22:34.774 --> 01:22:36.082
What are you doing?


01:22:36.083 --> 01:22:39.256
1200ccs, a dose half of this
size and I'm dead.


01:22:39.736 --> 01:22:43.380
It's times like this my temper
is tested somewhat.


01:22:43.381 --> 01:22:45.460
Maya, give me the injector.


01:22:45.461 --> 01:22:50.903
If I die Killian, what happens to your soldiers?
What happens to your product?


01:22:50.904 --> 01:22:52.103
We're not doing this, okay?


01:22:52.104 --> 01:22:54.545
What happens to you? What happens
if you go too hot?


01:23:08.073 --> 01:23:12.476
The good news is, a high level position
has just been vacated.


01:23:20.702 --> 01:23:23.722
-You're a maniac.
- No, I'm a visionary.


01:23:25.684 --> 01:23:30.246
But I do own a maniac, and he takes
the stage tonight.


01:23:33.968 --> 01:23:37.612
When we get the Iron Patriot, it'll take me
nine to ten minutes for a take down.


01:23:38.851 --> 01:23:41.173
That's great. The last time I looked
there was somebody inside of it.


01:23:47.656 --> 01:23:49.298
Afternoon, gentlemen.


01:23:52.339 --> 01:23:55.020
Hello Colonel.


01:23:55.021 --> 01:23:56.662
Step aside.


01:24:04.787 --> 01:24:07.550
We'll get you out of there,
don't worry.


01:24:07.751 --> 01:24:09.629
You'll damage the armor.


01:24:10.109 --> 01:24:13.912
Yes, I will, but you can
fix it, right?


01:24:14.792 --> 01:24:18.034
I'm going to take the suit up to base
camp, and I want Potts with me.


01:24:18.635 --> 01:24:20.756
She's still in Phase 2.


01:24:21.536 --> 01:24:24.058
You're not going deaf, are ya?


01:24:39.527 --> 01:24:41.608
Careful there, it's a limited edition.


01:24:42.129 --> 01:24:44.369
Hey, uh, ponytail express.


01:24:44.810 --> 01:24:47.851
What is the mileage count between Tennessee
and Miami? - 832 miles.


01:24:48.172 --> 01:24:50.213
Very nice.


01:24:51.774 --> 01:24:54.295
- Are you gonna stop that?
- Break it you bought it.


01:24:57.058 --> 01:25:00.252
Okay, that wasn't mine to give away, that
belongs to my friend's sister,


01:25:00.253 --> 01:25:03.502
and that's why I'm gonna
kill you first.


01:25:03.981 --> 01:25:05.102
- What're ya gonna do to me?
- You'll see.


01:25:05.502 --> 01:25:09.024
- You're zip-tied to a bed.
- This.


01:25:12.506 --> 01:25:13.947
That.


01:25:18.269 --> 01:25:19.711
Are you comin' out?


01:25:22.512 --> 01:25:26.674
Do not open, do not open, don't open, don't
open, don't- Alright, let's go.


01:25:33.958 --> 01:25:36.681
You breathe fire? Okay.


01:25:40.282 --> 01:25:43.284
It's a glorious day, Savin.


01:25:43.604 --> 01:25:49.248
This time tomorrow, I'll have the West's most
powerful leader in one hand.


01:25:49.249 --> 01:25:52.449
And the world's most feared
terrorist in the other.


01:25:53.290 --> 01:25:55.411
I'll own the War on Terror.


01:25:56.892 --> 01:26:01.776
Creates supply and demand for you
and your brothers and sisters.


01:26:04.937 --> 01:26:10.140
Trust me, you're going in a puddle of blood on
the ground in 5, 4, 3, Come on!, 2


01:26:12.701 --> 01:26:13.652
How did we get this shit?


01:26:13.653 --> 01:26:16.504
Alright, I'm going to give you a chance to
escape, put down your weapons.


01:26:17.504 --> 01:26:21.266
And tie yourselves into those chairs
and I'll let you live. In 5, 4


01:26:23.547 --> 01:26:26.001
You should be gone by now, you
should have already been gone.


01:26:26.002 --> 01:26:27.110
I'm just beyond terrified.


01:26:27.111 --> 01:26:28.589
Here it comes.


01:26:28.991 --> 01:26:30.593
3, 4


01:26:30.594 --> 01:26:32.593
Shut up. - 54321


01:26:33.392 --> 01:26:34.593
I told you.


01:26:47.561 --> 01:26:48.603
Where's the rest?


01:27:45.875 --> 01:27:49.878
Honestly, I hate working here...
they are so weird.


01:27:55.562 --> 01:27:56.802
Better late than never.


01:28:02.809 --> 01:28:04.569
Not this time. Not the face.


01:28:06.427 --> 01:28:08.723
Phew, it's good to be back. Hello,
by the way.


01:28:08.724 --> 01:28:09.519
Oh, hello sir.


01:28:15.643 --> 01:28:17.956
All personnel, Stark is loose and
somewhere in the compound.


01:28:17.957 --> 01:28:19.965
Repeat: Stark is loose and somewhere
in the compound.


01:28:22.220 --> 01:28:23.781
Ah, crap.


01:28:36.188 --> 01:28:38.749
- Tony.
- Rudy, tell me that was you in the suit.


01:28:38.769 --> 01:28:40.049
No, you got yours?


01:28:40.050 --> 01:28:43.312
Uh, um, kind of. Main house
as fast as you can.


01:28:43.353 --> 01:28:44.633
Somebody I'd like you to meet.


01:28:50.085 --> 01:28:52.106
You, you. Move!
Get out!


01:28:52.107 --> 01:28:54.079
The room is secure. I have eyes
on the Mandarin.


01:28:54.380 --> 01:28:56.589
What's this? I had winner's.


01:29:04.988 --> 01:29:06.195
What've you come as?


01:29:06.196 --> 01:29:08.431
Make a move and I'll break
your face.


01:29:09.911 --> 01:29:13.393
I never thought people had been hurt.
They lied to me.


01:29:14.074 --> 01:29:15.295
This is the Mandarin?


01:29:15.296 --> 01:29:17.155
I know, it's, it's embarrassing.


01:29:17.156 --> 01:29:19.117
Hi, I'm Trevor,
Trevor Slattery.


01:29:19.118 --> 01:29:23.053
I know I'm shorter in person, I'm a bit small,
everyone says that but, uh, hey


01:29:23.054 --> 01:29:26.600
if you're here to arrest me, there are
some people who I'd like to roll on.


01:29:26.601 --> 01:29:27.781
Here's how it works,
Meryl Streep.


01:29:27.782 --> 01:29:29.602
You tell him where Pepper
is and he'll stop doing it.


01:29:30.242 --> 01:29:33.564
Doing what? Oh, I get it! Ow!
That hurt! I get it! I get it!


01:29:33.565 --> 01:29:37.487
I do not know about any Pepper,
but I know the plan.


01:29:37.488 --> 01:29:39.649
- Spill.
- Do you know what they did to my suit?


01:29:40.008 --> 01:29:43.594
What? No. But I do know what's happening
off the coast.


01:29:43.595 --> 01:29:47.372
Something to do with uh... a big boat.
I can take you there.


01:29:51.536 --> 01:29:54.057
Tony, I swear to God, I'm going
to blow his face off.


01:29:54.058 --> 01:29:57.578
Oh this next bit may include the
Vice President as well.


01:29:58.620 --> 01:30:00.375
- Is that important?
- Somewhat.


01:30:00.376 --> 01:30:01.662
Yeah, a little bit.


01:30:04.847 --> 01:30:06.552
- So?
- Uh, what are we gonna do.


01:30:07.153 --> 01:30:10.370
We don't have any transport.


01:30:11.392 --> 01:30:14.795
Hey, Ringo, didn't you say something
about a "lovely speedboat"?


01:30:17.216 --> 01:30:19.665
If he's right about the location, we're 20 minutes
from where Pepper is.


01:30:19.666 --> 01:30:21.880
But we also have to figure out this
Vice President thing, right?


01:30:22.361 --> 01:30:25.202
I wonder who I'm calling right now.
Oh, that's the Vice President.


01:30:27.123 --> 01:30:29.643
- Hello.
- Sir, this is Tony Stark.


01:30:30.325 --> 01:30:31.713
Welcome back to the land
of the living.


01:30:31.714 --> 01:30:33.954
We believe you're about to be drawn
into the Mandarin campaign,


01:30:33.955 --> 01:30:36.089
and we've got to get you somewhere safe
as soon as possible.


01:30:36.168 --> 01:30:40.851
Mr. Stark, I'm about to eat honey roast ham
surrounded by the agency's finest.


01:30:40.852 --> 01:30:43.952
And the President is safe on Air Force One
with Colonel Rhodes.


01:30:44.052 --> 01:30:45.514
I think we're good here.


01:30:45.515 --> 01:30:47.454
Sir, this is Colonel Rhodes!


01:30:47.595 --> 01:30:49.473
They're using the Iron Patriot
as a trojan horse.


01:30:49.574 --> 01:30:50.436
They're gonna take out


01:30:50.437 --> 01:30:53.098
the President somehow. We have to
immediately alert that plane.


01:30:53.298 --> 01:30:55.799
Okay, I'm on it. I'll have security
lock it down. If need be,


01:30:55.800 --> 01:30:58.982
they can have F22s in the air in 30 seconds.
Thank you, Colonel.


01:30:59.080 --> 01:30:59.974
Rhodes and Stark out.


01:31:01.883 --> 01:31:03.200
Everything okay, sir?


01:31:04.702 --> 01:31:06.225
Couldn't be better.


01:31:12.910 --> 01:31:15.571
I love you, baby.


01:31:34.962 --> 01:31:38.023
Colonel Rhodes. Glad to see
you could make it, son.


01:31:38.125 --> 01:31:39.206
I feel safer already.


01:31:44.808 --> 01:31:46.089
We gotta make a decision.
We can either save


01:31:46.090 --> 01:31:48.090
the President or Pepper.
We can't do both.


01:31:48.310 --> 01:31:49.991
Sir, I have an update
from Malibu.


01:31:50.291 --> 01:31:52.197
The cranes have finally
arrived and the


01:31:52.198 --> 01:31:54.294
cellar doors are being
cleared as we speak.


01:31:54.854 --> 01:31:56.275
And what about the suit
I'm wearing?


01:31:56.276 --> 01:31:57.976
The armor is now at 92%.


01:31:59.035 --> 01:32:00.356
That's gonna have to do.


01:32:10.023 --> 01:32:11.752
Oh, here he comes, here he comes,
get a quick picture.


01:32:11.753 --> 01:32:12.184
Sure.


01:32:30.114 --> 01:32:32.037
Is everything all right,
Colonel?


01:33:02.853 --> 01:33:05.416
It is an honor,
Mr. President.


01:33:05.895 --> 01:33:08.237
If you're gonna do it,
do it.


01:33:08.437 --> 01:33:09.830
Woh. Cool your boots, Sir.


01:33:09.831 --> 01:33:11.759
That's not how the
Mandarin works.


01:33:11.829 --> 01:33:14.430
Sir. Air Force One's
been compromised.


01:33:14.570 --> 01:33:16.344
Internal shots, temperature
spikes.


01:33:16.345 --> 01:33:17.507
Get me eyes on it now.


01:33:17.508 --> 01:33:19.153
Image coming through
now, Sir.


01:33:21.836 --> 01:33:24.176
Is that Rhodes?


01:33:52.493 --> 01:33:55.493
The President.
Now.


01:33:55.975 --> 01:33:57.456
He's not here.


01:34:00.979 --> 01:34:02.943
Try the jet stream.


01:34:04.645 --> 01:34:06.741
Speaking of which,
go fish!


01:34:29.094 --> 01:34:31.535
Walk away from that, you
son of a bitch.


01:34:44.203 --> 01:34:46.845
- How many in the air?
- Thirteen, sir.


01:34:48.306 --> 01:34:50.106
- How many can I carry
- Four, sir.


01:35:00.113 --> 01:35:03.376
Slow down, slow down. Relax, what's
your name? Heather..


01:35:11.380 --> 01:35:13.914
Listen to me, see
that guy?


01:35:13.915 --> 01:35:15.333
I'm gonna swing
by him


01:35:15.334 --> 01:35:16.424
and you're just gonna
grab him.


01:35:16.624 --> 01:35:17.843
You got it?


01:35:19.806 --> 01:35:21.797
I will electrify your arm,


01:35:21.798 --> 01:35:23.566
you won't be able to open
your hand.


01:35:24.992 --> 01:35:26.192
You can do this,
Heather.


01:35:35.013 --> 01:35:37.754
Easy, see? Eleven
more to go.


01:35:40.616 --> 01:35:42.512
Remember that game called
Barrel of Monkeys?


01:35:42.513 --> 01:35:43.819
That's what we're
going to do.


01:35:43.820 --> 01:35:44.691
18,000 feet.


01:35:45.292 --> 01:35:47.261
Come on, people! Everybody, grab
your monkey!


01:35:51.942 --> 01:35:55.225
- Nice!
- 10,000 feet.


01:35:58.467 --> 01:36:00.428
- 6,000 feet.
- Come on, people.


01:36:01.269 --> 01:36:02.910
Come on, come on, come on


01:36:06.753 --> 01:36:10.115
- Yeah!
- 1000 feet.


01:36:11.635 --> 01:36:14.380
400 feet. 200 feet,
sir.


01:36:14.381 --> 01:36:16.258
It's a tricky monkey,
let's get him.


01:36:16.598 --> 01:36:18.359
Hello.


01:36:40.852 --> 01:36:42.581
Nice work guys.
Excellent.


01:36:42.582 --> 01:36:44.974
Good team effort all around.
Go us.


01:36:45.615 --> 01:36:48.136
Alright, Jarvis, but it's only half done,
we still gotta get Pepp-


01:36:56.141 --> 01:36:58.663
That came out of nowhere.


01:36:59.503 --> 01:37:00.420
Gimme some good
news man.


01:37:00.421 --> 01:37:01.925
- I think they all made it.
- Thank God.


01:37:02.144 --> 01:37:03.984
Yeah, but I missed the President.


01:37:04.386 --> 01:37:05.903
You couldn't save the President
with the suit,


01:37:05.904 --> 01:37:07.227
how are you gonna save Pepper
without it?


01:37:08.068 --> 01:37:09.999
Uh, say Jarvis, is it
that time?


01:37:10.000 --> 01:37:12.110
The "house party"
protocol, sir?


01:37:12.111 --> 01:37:13.211
Correct.


01:37:44.106 --> 01:37:45.986
Hi.


01:37:52.391 --> 01:37:56.893
You think he's gonna help you...
he won't.


01:38:01.636 --> 01:38:04.453
Having you here is not just
to motivate Tony Stark,


01:38:04.754 --> 01:38:07.820
it's actually more embarrassing
than that.


01:38:08.519 --> 01:38:13.322
- You're here as my, um
- Trophy.


01:38:25.289 --> 01:38:27.409
Good evening, sir.


01:38:31.413 --> 01:38:33.334
Welcome aboard,
Mr. President.


01:38:42.659 --> 01:38:45.384
You ever heard of an elephant
graveyard?


01:38:45.385 --> 01:38:49.663
Well, two years ago, the elephant in
the room was this scow.


01:38:52.414 --> 01:38:53.374
This is the Roxxon Norco.


01:38:53.674 --> 01:38:57.077
Of course you remember when she spilled 100
million gallons of crude off Pensacola.


01:38:57.136 --> 01:38:59.698
Thanks to you, not one fat
cat saw a day in court.


01:39:00.278 --> 01:39:01.599
What do you want from me?


01:39:02.800 --> 01:39:04.542
Uh, nothing, sir.


01:39:04.581 --> 01:39:07.704
I just needed a reason to kill you
that would play well on TV.


01:39:08.272 --> 01:39:12.835
You see, I've moved on. I've found myself
a new political patron, and


01:39:13.055 --> 01:39:15.536
At this time tomorrow, he'll
have your job.


01:39:17.237 --> 01:39:18.938
String him up.


01:39:37.509 --> 01:39:38.770
Come on.


01:39:43.232 --> 01:39:44.994
You're not gonna freak out
on me, right?


01:39:44.995 --> 01:39:45.554
I hope not.


01:40:11.649 --> 01:40:13.190
Oh my God.


01:40:14.672 --> 01:40:17.039
He's strung up over the oil tank, they're
gonna light him up, man.


01:40:17.040 --> 01:40:18.093
Viking funeral.


01:40:18.553 --> 01:40:21.315
- Public execution.
- Yeah, death by oil.


01:40:27.597 --> 01:40:30.679
Broadcast will commence shortly.
Take final positions.


01:40:31.820 --> 01:40:33.028
Okay, that's good.


01:40:33.029 --> 01:40:35.902
Now give me cameras A through E
and we'll do a full tech rehearsal.


01:40:37.986 --> 01:40:39.072
Is your gun up?


01:40:39.497 --> 01:40:40.991
Yup, what do I do?


01:40:40.992 --> 01:40:43.721
Stay on my six, cover high, and don't
shoot me in the back.


01:40:43.722 --> 01:40:45.094
Six, high, back. Alright.


01:40:55.253 --> 01:40:56.356
You see that? Nailed it.


01:40:56.357 --> 01:40:58.056
Yeah, you really killed
the glass.


01:40:58.057 --> 01:40:59.174
I was aiming for the bulb?


01:40:59.175 --> 01:41:00.637
You can't hit a bulb from
this distance.


01:41:05.339 --> 01:41:07.665
I'm out. Gimme, gimme, you got
an extra magazine?


01:41:07.666 --> 01:41:08.940
They're not universal, Tony.


01:41:09.262 --> 01:41:10.571
I know what I'm doing, I make this stuff.
Gimme another one.


01:41:11.434 --> 01:41:13.025
I don't have one that
fits that gun.


01:41:13.205 --> 01:41:13.728
You've got like five of them.


01:41:13.729 --> 01:41:15.886
Alright, here's what I'm gonna do.
I'm gonna spot. Ready?


01:41:16.887 --> 01:41:18.132
What'd you see?


01:41:18.133 --> 01:41:20.849
Too fast, nothing.
Here we go.


01:41:25.192 --> 01:41:27.153
Three guys, one girl,
all armed.


01:41:37.107 --> 01:41:38.802
God, I'd kill for some
armor right now.


01:41:38.803 --> 01:41:40.709
- You're right, we need backup.
- Yeah, much.


01:41:42.111 --> 01:41:44.010
You know what?


01:41:47.473 --> 01:41:49.034
- Is that?
- Yep.


01:41:50.516 --> 01:41:51.635
- Are those?
- Yeah.


01:42:08.965 --> 01:42:10.406
Merry Christmas, buddy.


01:42:15.569 --> 01:42:17.952
Jarvis, target Extremis heat
signatures.


01:42:17.953 --> 01:42:19.740
Disable with extreme prejudice.


01:42:19.841 --> 01:42:21.213
Yes, sir.


01:42:25.775 --> 01:42:28.857
What are you waiting for?
It's Christmas.


01:42:30.418 --> 01:42:31.219
Take 'em to church.


01:42:52.832 --> 01:42:54.852
Jarvis, get Igor to steady
this thing.


01:43:07.119 --> 01:43:09.268
This is how you've been managing
your downtime, huh?


01:43:09.269 --> 01:43:10.321
Everybody needs a hobby.


01:43:16.685 --> 01:43:18.726
Heartbreaker? Help Red Snapper
out, will ya?


01:43:46.984 --> 01:43:47.536
Nice timing.


01:43:47.537 --> 01:43:49.744
Oh yeah, that's awesome. Give me
a suit, okay?


01:43:51.907 --> 01:43:53.707
Oh, I'm sorry. They're
only coded to me.


01:43:54.107 --> 01:43:54.894
What's that mean?


01:43:54.895 --> 01:43:55.868
I got you covered.


01:43:59.590 --> 01:44:02.792
- Good evening, Colonel. Can I give you a lift?
- Very funny.


01:44:20.603 --> 01:44:22.885
- Sir, I've located Miss Potts.
- About time.


01:44:35.691 --> 01:44:38.614
Stop, put it down, put it
down, put it down.


01:44:41.254 --> 01:44:43.256
See what happens when you hang out
with my ex-girlfriends?


01:44:46.137 --> 01:44:47.006
You're such a jerk.


01:44:47.007 --> 01:44:48.619
Yup, we'll talk about
it at dinner.


01:44:50.459 --> 01:44:53.181
Come on, a little more,
baby.


01:45:09.031 --> 01:45:10.472
Is this guy bothering you?


01:45:12.032 --> 01:45:14.755
Don't get up!


01:45:17.756 --> 01:45:19.717
Is it hot there?


01:45:21.078 --> 01:45:22.758
Stuck? Feel a little stuck?


01:45:23.759 --> 01:45:27.041
Like a little turtle, cooking in
his little turtle suit?


01:45:27.641 --> 01:45:29.242
Tony


01:45:29.243 --> 01:45:30.884
She's watching.


01:45:32.085 --> 01:45:33.606
I think you should close
your eyes.


01:45:33.607 --> 01:45:34.606
Close your eyes.


01:45:35.206 --> 01:45:38.168
Close your eyes. You don't
want to see this.


01:45:45.613 --> 01:45:47.133
Yeah, you take a minute.


01:46:20.192 --> 01:46:21.874
Jarvis, give me a suit
right now!


01:46:32.840 --> 01:46:34.440
Aw, come on!


01:46:35.841 --> 01:46:38.803
Mr. President! Just hold on,
alright? I'm coming.


01:46:40.084 --> 01:46:42.325
Just hold on.
Hold on.


01:47:04.138 --> 01:47:05.598
Buh-bye.


01:47:17.305 --> 01:47:19.067
Brace yourself!


01:47:29.553 --> 01:47:33.235
You look damn good, Mr. President, but
I'm gonna need that suit back.


01:47:46.323 --> 01:47:48.404
The President is secure, Tony.
I'm clearing the area.


01:47:48.405 --> 01:47:49.419
Nice work.


01:47:49.921 --> 01:47:51.765
- Ready sir?
- What do you mean "ready"?


01:48:00.732 --> 01:48:04.972
Pep, I got you. Relax, I got you.
Just look at me.


01:48:06.854 --> 01:48:09.452
Honey, I can't reach any further, and
you can't stay there, alright?


01:48:09.453 --> 01:48:10.477
You gotta let go.


01:48:10.576 --> 01:48:13.379
You gotta let go. I'll catch
you, I promise.


01:48:43.876 --> 01:48:47.759
What a shame, I would
have caught her.


01:49:18.069 --> 01:49:19.170
Eject.


01:50:04.844 --> 01:50:07.285
Well here we are,
on the roof.


01:50:17.651 --> 01:50:19.452
- Mark 42 inbound.
- Well I'll be damned.


01:50:20.252 --> 01:50:21.813
The prodigal son returns.


01:50:37.983 --> 01:50:39.143
Whatever.


01:50:40.144 --> 01:50:42.024
You really didn't deserve
her, Tony.


01:50:43.267 --> 01:50:47.028
It's a pity. I was so close to having
her... perfect.


01:50:49.890 --> 01:50:52.116
Okay, okay, wait, wait, slow down,
slow down.


01:50:52.417 --> 01:50:54.352
You're right. I don't
deserve her.


01:50:55.633 --> 01:50:57.154
But here's where
you're wrong.


01:50:57.874 --> 01:51:00.236
She was already perfect.


01:51:06.799 --> 01:51:11.221
Jarvis, do me a favor and
blow Mark 42.


01:51:11.344 --> 01:51:15.258
NOOOO!!


01:52:26.686 --> 01:52:28.646
No more false faces.


01:52:29.228 --> 01:52:31.627
You said you wanted
the Mandarin.


01:52:32.228 --> 01:52:34.331
You're looking right
at him.


01:52:35.332 --> 01:52:38.770
It was always me, Tony, right
from the start.


01:52:38.971 --> 01:52:40.514
I am the Mandarin!


01:52:51.981 --> 01:52:53.702
I got nothing.


01:52:59.545 --> 01:53:02.707
Jarvis, subject at my 12 o'clock
is not a target, disengage!


01:53:11.272 --> 01:53:13.313
What? Oh what, are
you mad at me?


01:53:38.688 --> 01:53:39.949
Honey.


01:53:44.612 --> 01:53:45.872
Oh my God.


01:53:47.273 --> 01:53:49.755
I was really violent.


01:53:50.515 --> 01:53:53.050
You just scared the devil out of me.
I thought you were


01:53:53.051 --> 01:53:55.458
I was dead. Why? Because I
fell two hundred feet?


01:53:58.220 --> 01:54:02.163
- Who's the hot mess now?
- Still debatable.


01:54:03.223 --> 01:54:04.392
Probably tipping your way
a little bit.


01:54:04.393 --> 01:54:05.504
Why don't you dress like
this at home?


01:54:06.065 --> 01:54:08.065
Hmm? Sports bra, the
whole deal.


01:54:08.406 --> 01:54:11.607
You know I think I understand why you
don't want to give up the suits.


01:54:12.189 --> 01:54:14.149
What I am gonna complain
about now?


01:54:15.509 --> 01:54:18.991
Well, it's me. I'll think
of something.


01:54:20.593 --> 01:54:23.634
- Don't touch me. No, I'm gonna burn you!
- No, no.


01:54:24.776 --> 01:54:26.376
You're not hot.


01:54:27.396 --> 01:54:29.078
Am I gonna be okay?


01:54:29.079 --> 01:54:32.240
No, you're in a relationship with me,
everything will never be okay.


01:54:33.160 --> 01:54:35.081
But I think I can figure
this out, yeah.


01:54:35.082 --> 01:54:39.565
I almost had this 20 years ago when I was
drunk. I think I can get you better.


01:54:40.723 --> 01:54:42.325
That's what I do.
I fix things.


01:54:43.566 --> 01:54:45.767
And all your distractions?


01:54:46.168 --> 01:54:48.409
Uh, I'm gonna shave them
down a little bit.


01:54:48.410 --> 01:54:51.956
- Jarvis, hey.
- All wrapped up here, sir.


01:54:51.957 --> 01:54:54.412
Will there be anything else?


01:54:54.413 --> 01:54:55.413
You know what to do.


01:54:56.113 --> 01:54:58.895
The "clean slate" protocol,
sir?


01:54:58.896 --> 01:55:02.197
Screw it, it's Christmas.
Yes, yes.


01:55:38.838 --> 01:55:40.940
Okay so far?
You like it?


01:55:42.440 --> 01:55:44.522
It'll do.


01:55:52.486 --> 01:55:57.409
And so, as Christmas morning began, my
journey had reached its end.


01:56:01.812 --> 01:56:06.094
You start with something pure,
something exciting.


01:56:06.775 --> 01:56:09.536
Then come the mistakes.


01:56:10.297 --> 01:56:12.218
The compromises.


01:56:18.501 --> 01:56:20.863
"We create our own Demons".


01:56:26.427 --> 01:56:28.427
It's great to see you.


01:56:33.277 --> 01:56:35.980
Of course, there are people who
say progress is dangerous.


01:56:36.479 --> 01:56:39.881
But I'll bet none of those idiots ever had to live
with a chest full of shrapnel.


01:56:40.442 --> 01:56:43.344
And now... neither will I.


01:56:44.363 --> 01:56:48.125
Let me tell you, that was the best
sleep I'd had in years.


01:57:09.149 --> 01:57:12.911
- It's okay, it's okay.
- No!


01:58:30.678 --> 01:58:34.200
So if I were to wrap this up tight
with a bow or whatever.


01:58:34.358 --> 01:58:40.783
I guess I'd say my armor was never
a distraction or a hobby.


01:58:41.304 --> 01:58:43.224
It was a cocoon.


01:58:44.245 --> 01:58:49.247
And now, I'm a
changed man.


01:58:58.294 --> 01:59:00.474
You can take away
my house,


01:59:00.874 --> 01:59:02.314
All my tricks and toys.


01:59:02.895 --> 01:59:05.098
One thing you can't take away...


01:59:08.259 --> 01:59:10.361
I am Iron Man.


02:08:51.554 --> 02:08:53.856
You know, and thank you, by
the way, for listening.


02:08:53.857 --> 02:08:56.845
There's just something about getting
it off my chest and putting


02:08:56.846 --> 02:08:59.559
it out there in the atmosphere
instead of holding this in.


02:08:59.889 --> 02:09:02.791
I mean, this is what gets people
sick, you know?


02:09:02.991 --> 02:09:05.893
Wow, I had no idea you were
such a good listener.


02:09:05.993 --> 02:09:09.603
To be able to share all of my intimate
thoughts and my experiences


02:09:09.604 --> 02:09:12.897
with someone, it just cuts the weight
of it in half, you know.


02:09:12.898 --> 02:09:14.252
It's like a snake swallowing
its own tail.


02:09:14.354 --> 02:09:15.298
Everything comes full circle.


02:09:15.798 --> 02:09:18.700
And...and the fact that you've been
able to help me process-


02:09:21.272 --> 02:09:22.672
- So, uh...?
- You with me?


02:09:22.673 --> 02:09:24.874
I was, yeah. Mm-hmm. We were...
uh, we were at, uh...


02:09:24.875 --> 02:09:26.274
You actively napping?


02:09:26.275 --> 02:09:28.676
I...I was...I... I...
I drifted.


02:09:28.976 --> 02:09:30.277
Where did I lose you?


02:09:32.078 --> 02:09:34.379
Elevator in Switzerland.


02:09:35.180 --> 02:09:36.480
So you heard none of it?


02:09:36.981 --> 02:09:40.203
I'm sorry, I'm not that
kind of doctor.


02:09:40.204 --> 02:09:42.884
I'm not a therapist, it's not
my training.


02:09:42.885 --> 02:09:44.285
- So?
- I don't have the...


02:09:44.385 --> 02:09:46.987
- What? The time?
- Temperament.


02:09:47.087 --> 02:09:49.122
You know what? Now that I
think about it,


02:09:49.123 --> 02:09:52.690
Oh God my original wound.
1983, alright?


02:09:52.691 --> 02:09:53.390
Yes.


02:09:53.391 --> 02:09:56.092
I'm 14 years old, I still have a nanny?
That was weird.
